INSERT INTO `devblogs` VALUES ('day-01','01','Genesis of the System: Topic Selection, Architecture Drafting & Pure PHP Foundations','August 26, 2026','Kicked off on topic selection day—immediately drafted the architecture, cataloged requirements, explored UI inspirations, and began non-stop coding during every free hour adhering strictly to pure PHP with zero static HTML.','{"id":"day-01","sprint_number":"01","sprint_badge":"DAY 01 · TOPIC SELECTION & SYSTEM DRAFTING","title":"Genesis of the System: Topic Selection, Architecture Drafting & Pure PHP Foundations","date":"August 26, 2026","read_time":"5 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Kicked off on topic selection day—immediately drafted the architecture, cataloged requirements, explored UI inspirations, and began non-stop coding during every free hour adhering strictly to pure PHP with zero static HTML.","tags":["Topic Selection","System Blueprint","Modular PHP","Zero Static HTML"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-01.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>Our journey began on August 26, 2026—the day our team picked the project topic for our COAL101 Web Systems and Technologies midterm lab project.</p><p>As soon as we chose the <strong>Campus Job Posting System</strong>, we didn''t waste a single moment. We planned immediately, structured the project directory hierarchy, listed every functional module we would need, and researched modern design inspirations suited for a premier institutional portal.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-code-slash text-accent me-2''></i>Strict Stack Compliance: Native PHP, No Raw HTML</h5><p>During our free time that day on campus, we started drafting the site. We strictly limited our stack to what our professor permitted: Native PHP, CSS, Bootstrap 5.3, and Vanilla JavaScript—with <strong>strictly no standalone HTML files</strong> as our professor instructed. Every page had to be dynamically composed via modular PHP components.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-lightning-charge-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Lead Developer Dedication</h5><p>As the lead of this development, I simply couldn''t stop thinking about the system. I continued developing through another free period that same day and kept writing code up until we went home, determined to finish the foundational task.</p>","key_takeaways":["Selected the Campus Job Posting System topic and mapped all functional requirements.","Enforced pure Native PHP modular template architecture with zero static .html files.","Defined initial JSON datastore schemas for users, categories, jobs, and applications.","Developed continuously through campus free periods and after going home to build the skeleton."],"tech_stack":["Native PHP 8","Bootstrap 5.3","Modular Architecture","JSON Datastore Schema"]}','2026-08-25 12:00:00'),('day-02','02','The Start of the Madness: All-Day Coding Sprint & 1:00 AM Optimization Marathon','August 27, 2026','Pushed through an intensive full-day coding marathon from early morning to 1:00 AM—building the zero-DB JSON persistence engine, session state synchronization, password entropy meter, and end-to-end application workflows.','{"id":"day-02","sprint_number":"02","sprint_badge":"DAY 02 · DEEP DIVE & CODING MARATHON","title":"The Start of the Madness: All-Day Coding Sprint & 1:00 AM Optimization Marathon","date":"August 27, 2026","read_time":"6 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Pushed through an intensive full-day coding marathon from early morning to 1:00 AM—building the zero-DB JSON persistence engine, session state synchronization, password entropy meter, and end-to-end application workflows.","tags":["Coding Marathon","JSON Engine","Session Sync","Password Entropy"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-02.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>August 27 was the true start of creating this madness. The moment I woke up in the morning, I jumped directly into the codebase to develop and optimize the core architecture even further.</p><p>For the entire day, I worked non-stop on our zero-database data architecture. I built <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>includes/data-helper.php</code>, establishing atomic file reads/writes for our JSON datasets and synchronizing live states into <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>$_SESSION</code> for zero database overhead and lightning-fast responses.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-shield-lock-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Security Algorithms & Shift Availability Matrix</h5><p>I engineered the standalone client-side Shannon password entropy analyzer (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>password-strength.js</code>) with real-time criteria checkmarks, role-based access control (RBAC), and built the interactive 18-slot weekly schedule availability time grid matrix for student job submissions.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-moon-stars-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Pushing Through to 1:00 AM</h5><p>I coded and optimized straight through the evening and night, finally stopping at 1:00 AM on August 28, hoping that this intensive development foundation would be solid and comprehensive enough for our project.</p>","key_takeaways":["Engineered zero-database atomic JSON persistence and dynamic session synchronization.","Implemented real-time client-side password entropy scoring and visual strength feedback.","Built the 18-slot weekly schedule availability grid matrix for student applications.","Completed a grueling 16+ hour coding marathon ending at 1:00 AM for core engine stability."],"tech_stack":["Native PHP 8","Atomic JSON Engine","Shannon Entropy Algorithm","Session Persistence"]}','2026-08-26 12:00:00'),('day-03','03','Team Git Collaboration, Mentoring Groupmates & The Dual-Design Strategy','August 28, 2026','Balanced multi-subject coursework with core development, mentored groupmates on Git and GitHub collaborative workflows, and initiated a dual-design strategy to present two strong prototypes to our professor.','{"id":"day-03","sprint_number":"03","sprint_badge":"DAY 03 · GIT ONBOARDING & DUAL DESIGN","title":"Team Git Collaboration, Mentoring Groupmates & The Dual-Design Strategy","date":"August 28, 2026","read_time":"6 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Balanced multi-subject coursework with core development, mentored groupmates on Git and GitHub collaborative workflows, and initiated a dual-design strategy to present two strong prototypes to our professor.","tags":["Git Collaboration","Team Mentoring","Dual Design","UX Critique"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-03.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>When I woke up in the morning, well what do you expect—I quickly finished my required tasks for other subjects and immediately dove straight back into system development.</p><p>Today marked a major team milestone: I conducted a hands-on mentoring session for my groupmates to teach them how the system works, how our file hierarchy is organized, and how to use <strong>Git and GitHub for collaborative development</strong>. They learned remarkably fast and were eager to contribute.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-diagram-3-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Dual-Design Presentation Strategy</h5><p>To maximize our impact during the midterm presentation, we planned a dual-design strategy: my groupmates would develop their design variation, while I developed mine. This ensures we can present 2 distinct, fully functioning design directions to our professor.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-clock-history text-accent me-2''></i>The 11:30 PM Build & UX Reflections</h5><p>I completed that day''s development build at 11:30 PM. However, stepping back to evaluate it, my design still felt incomplete and the UX did not fully satisfy my standards. I resolved then and there to start developing further tomorrow to bring the user experience to perfection.</p>","key_takeaways":["Taught groupmates Git version control and GitHub collaborative repository workflows.","Established the dual-design strategy to develop and present 2 unique prototype options.","Completed the 11:30 PM core build milestone covering applicant review and admin controls.","Critiqued UX shortcomings and established high-fidelity refinement goals for the next day."],"tech_stack":["Git & GitHub Workflows","Collaborative Branching","Bootstrap 5.3 Modals","PHP State Handlers"]}','2026-08-27 12:00:00'),('day-04','04','Perfecting the Tactile Paper Sheet UX: Spotlight Search, 3D DevBlog & Final Polish','August 29, 2026','Following up on yesterday''s UX critique, elevated the portal experience—crafting the signature Tactile Paper Sheet design system, keyboard-driven spotlight search (Ctrl+K), and interactive 3D DevBlog Coverflow.','{"id":"day-04","sprint_number":"04","sprint_badge":"DAY 04 · TACTILE UX & SYSTEM HARMONY","title":"Perfecting the Tactile Paper Sheet UX: Spotlight Search, 3D DevBlog & Final Polish","date":"August 29, 2026","read_time":"5 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Following up on yesterday''s UX critique, elevated the portal experience—crafting the signature Tactile Paper Sheet design system, keyboard-driven spotlight search (Ctrl+K), and interactive 3D DevBlog Coverflow.","tags":["Tactile UX","Spotlight Search","Design System","Final Polish"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-04.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>Following up on yesterday''s self-critique where the UX still felt incomplete, today''s objective was relentless visual and interactive perfection.</p><p>I dedicated today to turning raw functional components into a unified, tactile experience. We established the <strong>Tactile Paper Sheet Design System</strong>, introducing warm ivory canvas tones (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>#FBF9F4</code>), deep carbon ink contrast (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>#161616</code>), physical paper border elevations, and official KLD Green accents across all student, employer, and administrative views.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-search text-accent me-2''></i>Universal Spotlight Search & 3D Stage DevBlog</h5><p>To make navigation effortless, I engineered the keyboard-driven universal Spotlight Search modal (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>Ctrl+K</code>) that queries <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>api/search-jobs.php</code> with live debouncing. Furthermore, I built this interactive 3D Coverflow DevBlog on the About Us page so our entire daily journey is recorded transparently for our professor and peers.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-check-all text-accent me-2''></i>Presentation Readiness</h5><p>With both design variations prepared and our core workflows rigorously validated across mobile and desktop devices, we are fully prepared to present our dual-design project to our professor with utmost confidence.</p>","key_takeaways":["Perfected the Tactile Paper Sheet design tokens across all student, employer, and admin interfaces.","Engineered universal Spotlight Search (Ctrl+K) with live API debounce.","Constructed the interactive 3D perspective DevBlog Coverflow and modal reader.","Ensured both design variations are polished and presentation-ready for our professor."],"tech_stack":["CSS3 3D Perspective","Spotlight Search API","Tactile Paper Tokens","Vanilla JS ES6"]}','2026-08-28 12:00:00'),('day-05','05','Enterprise MySQL Migration: Relational Schema, ACID Migrations & Full-Width 100vh Hero Viewport','September 02, 2026','Migrated the entire data persistence architecture from flat-file JSON to MySQL (PDO) with ACID migrations, expanded the viewport to 100% full-width with a 100vh landing hero, and verified all 106 Playwright tests.','{"id":"day-05","sprint_number":"05","sprint_badge":"DAY 05 · ENTERPRISE MYSQL & 100VH HERO","title":"Enterprise MySQL Migration: Relational Schema, ACID Migrations & Full-Width 100vh Hero Viewport","date":"September 02, 2026","read_time":"6 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Migrated the entire data persistence architecture from flat-file JSON to MySQL (PDO) with ACID migrations, expanded the viewport to 100% full-width with a 100vh landing hero, and verified all 106 Playwright tests.","tags":["MySQL Migration","PDO Prepared Statements","ACID Transactions","100vh Viewport"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-05.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>Flat-file JSON persistence carried our prototype through early milestones, but enterprise scalability and concurrent applicant handling demanded a true relational database.</p><p>Today marked our largest architectural leap: migrating the data layer to <strong>MySQL/MariaDB via PHP Data Objects (PDO)</strong>. I established <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>includes/db.php</code> as a secure PDO connection singleton and performed a complete rewrite of <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>includes/data-helper.php</code>. Every read, write, filter, and state transition now executes via parameterized SQL queries, completely eliminating SQL injection risks and multi-process file concurrency race conditions.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-arrow-repeat text-accent me-2''></i>ACID Database Migration & Seeding Engine</h5><p>I built <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>database/schema.sql</code> and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>database/migrate.php</code>, creating an automated CLI and browser migration runner. The engine wraps schema initialization, table truncations, and JSON seed data re-import into a single atomic ACID transaction, enabling instantaneous database resets without schema corruption.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-aspect-ratio text-accent me-2''></i>100vh Hero Section & Full-Width Paper Sheet</h5><p>I expanded the portal canvas by removing artificial max-width constraints on <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>.sheet</code> for a 100% full-width layout. I constructed an expansive 100vh full-screen landing hero section with vertically centered typography, elevated partner strips, and split student registration name fields (First, Middle, Last). Ran our entire automated Playwright test suite—achieving 106/106 passed tests with zero regressions!</p>","key_takeaways":["Replaced flat-file JSON storage with enterprise MySQL (PDO) prepared statements across all queries.","Engineered transactional CLI/web database migration engine (database/migrate.php).","Expanded portal layout to full-width with an immersive 100vh hero viewport and split name fields.","Achieved 100% pass rate across 106 automated Playwright E2E test specs on the new relational engine."],"tech_stack":["PHP Data Objects (PDO)","MySQL 8 / MariaDB","ACID Migration Engine","100vh Full-Width Layout","Playwright E2E Suite"]}','2026-09-01 12:00:00'),('day-06','06','Relational Foreign Keys, Swarm Security Hardening & Permanent Demo/Real Data Coexistence','September 03, 2026','Implemented explicit MySQL foreign key constraints with EER semantic labels, conducted a comprehensive swarm security audit hardening MIME types and IDOR boundaries, and unified demo/real datastores for permanent coexistence.','{"id":"day-06","sprint_number":"06","sprint_badge":"DAY 06 · RELATIONAL INTEGRITY & DEFENSE-IN-DEPTH","title":"Relational Foreign Keys, Swarm Security Hardening & Permanent Demo/Real Data Coexistence","date":"September 03, 2026","read_time":"6 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Implemented explicit MySQL foreign key constraints with EER semantic labels, conducted a comprehensive swarm security audit hardening MIME types and IDOR boundaries, and unified demo/real datastores for permanent coexistence.","tags":["Relational Integrity","Foreign Keys","Swarm Security Audit","IDOR Protection"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-06.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>With MySQL fully active, today was dedicated to relational modeling rigor, database constraint enforcement, and ironclad defense-in-depth security.</p><p>I enhanced <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>database/schema.sql</code> with explicit semantic foreign key constraints (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>fk_jobs_category</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>fk_jobs_employer</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>fk_apps_job</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>fk_apps_student</code>) and added <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>UNIQUE KEY unique_student_job</code> to prevent duplicate submissions at the relational level.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-shield-lock text-accent me-2''></i>Swarm Security Audit & Defensive Hardening</h5><p>I executed a comprehensive security audit across all entry points: whitelisted registration roles strictly to <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>[''student'', ''employer'']</code> preventing privilege escalation to admin,('day-27','27','Frictionless Candidate Mobility: Stored Profile Resumes, Automated Application Binding, Concurrent Placement Governance & Balanced Settings Ergonomics','October 4, 2026','Engineered end-to-end candidate mobility and institutional appointment safeguards across the platform: introduced persistent student profile resumes with automatic application binding and self-service settings management; established real-time concurrent placement pipeline tracking and automated application withdrawal cascades to enforce campus 20-hour workload limits; and executed a comprehensive UI/UX overhaul of the settings center to achieve perfect dual-column baseline symmetry with zero dead space.','{"id":"day-27","sprint_number":"27","sprint_badge":"DAY 27 · PERSISTENT PROFILE RESUMES, APPLICATION AUTO-LINKING, CONCURRENT PLACEMENT GOVERNANCE & SETTINGS UI/UX REBALANCING","title":"Frictionless Candidate Mobility: Stored Profile Resumes, Automated Application Binding, Concurrent Placement Governance & Balanced Settings Ergonomics","date":"October 4, 2026","read_time":"10 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Engineered end-to-end candidate mobility and institutional appointment safeguards across the platform: introduced persistent student profile resumes with automatic application binding and self-service settings management; established real-time concurrent placement pipeline tracking and automated application withdrawal cascades to enforce campus 20-hour workload limits; and executed a comprehensive UI/UX overhaul of the settings center to achieve perfect dual-column baseline symmetry with zero dead space.","tags":["Persistent Profile Resumes","Application Auto-Linking","Runtime Schema Evolution","Concurrent Placement Tracking","Auto-Withdrawal Cascade","Institutional Work Safeguards","Settings UI/UX Overhaul","Zero-Dead-Space Layout"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-27.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>Day 27 marks a defining milestone in candidate experience and institutional hiring integrity across the KLD Campus Job Posting System. We eliminated candidate friction by introducing persistent student profile resumes with automated application binding, solved cross-department hiring conflicts through concurrent placement tracking and automated withdrawal cascades, and resolved an ergonomic layout imbalance in our centralized settings center to deliver a pristine, zero-dead-space dual-column user interface.</p><p>As university operations scale across multiple academic institutes and administrative units, candidate mobility must be seamless for students while remaining strictly compliant with institutional work regulations. Today''s sprint addresses both sides of this equation—empowering students with effortless application submission while arming departmental supervisors with complete placement transparency and automated policy enforcement.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-file-earmark-person-fill text-accent me-2''></i>1. Persistent Student Profile Resumes &amp; Frictionless Auto-Linking</h5><p>In earlier iterations of our student job application workflow (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>student/apply.php</code>), the submission form promised: <em>''You may attach an updated PDF or leave blank to automatically link your stored student profile resume.''</em> However, an architectural audit revealed that student resumes were previously treated solely as ephemeral, single-application attachments without any backing persistence in the student profile schema. Students were forced to re-upload their CV for every vacancy, causing redundant file clutter on disk and unnecessary friction.</p><p>We resolved this by evolving our relational schema: we introduced <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>resume_file VARCHAR(255) NULL</code> to <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>student_profiles</code>, added automated runtime schema guarantees in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>DatastoreManager::ensureSchema()</code>, and mapped proper SQL bindings in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>database/migrate.php</code>. In <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>user-service.php</code>, we expanded profile update and query routines, implemented secure profile resume authorization via <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>can_access_resume_file()</code>, and ensured <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>hydrate_user()</code> automatically populates both <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>resume</code> and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>resume_file</code> aliases.</p><p>In the application view (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>student-apply-view.php</code>), leaving the resume upload blank now automatically resolves and binds the student''s stored CV to the application record, displaying a reassuring green active resume badge while still allowing candidates to upload an ad-hoc custom document whenever necessary.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-diagram-3-fill text-accent me-2''></i>2. Concurrent Placement Governance &amp; Automatic Withdrawal Cascade</h5><p>Under university guidelines and institutional labor policies, student assistantships are capped at a strict <strong>20-hour maximum per week</strong>, with students restricted to exactly <strong>one active campus appointment per academic term</strong>. Previously, an eager student could apply to multiple departments simultaneously, and if multiple supervisors issued acceptance offers concurrently, scheduling collisions and administrative confusion ensued.</p><p>To solve this, we engineered deep placement intelligence into <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>includes/services/application-service.php</code> via <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>ApplicationService::getStudentPlacementSummary()</code>. This engine analyzes a candidate''s complete application pipeline across all campus departments, checking whether the student already holds an accepted appointment or has active interviews underway. In <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>employer/review-app.php</code> and candidate applicant rosters, supervisors are now presented with real-time placement status pills (<em>''Active Placement Held''</em>, <em>''Evaluating in Other Departments''</em>) and contextual warnings before finalizing an offer.</p><p>Crucially, we implemented <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>auto_withdraw_other_applications()</code> in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>includes/services/job-service.php</code>. The moment any department supervisor accepts a candidate, the system executes an atomic transaction that transitions all other pending and under-review applications for that student to <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>withdrawn</code> status. The system appends an automated audit explanation to the supervisor notes (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>Auto-withdrawn: Candidate accepted position for [Job Title] ([Department])</code>) and dispatches real-time in-app notifications to both the student and all affected departmental hiring managers, preventing duplicate hiring locks across the institution.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-columns-gap text-accent me-2''></i>3. Settings Page Layout Ergonomics &amp; Zero-Dead-Space UI/UX Overhaul (/uipro)</h5><p>During visual audit reviews on high-resolution displays, our team detected an unsightly vertical imbalance in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>settings.php</code>. The left column (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>col-lg-7</code>) was heavily loaded with personal details, locked academic credentials, and the 18-slot weekly shift matrix, stretching downward over 1,600px. Meanwhile, the right column (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>col-lg-5</code>) had only password fields and a theme toggle wrapped inside a stretched flex container (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>card-paper h-100</code>). This created over 1,000px of barren, empty white space on the right side.</p><p>We executed a complete visual rebalancing adhering to our <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>/uipro</code> design standards:</p><ul><li><strong>Extracted Stored Profile Resume:</strong> Relocated the resume management interface out of the crowded left column and established it as a prominent, dedicated card at the top of the right column, complete with inline preview via <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>view-resume.php</code>, single-click removal, and quick file replacement.</li><li><strong>Decoupled Modular Containers:</strong> Divided the right column into three focused, clean cards: <em>Stored Profile Resume</em>, <em>Security &amp; Password</em>, and <em>Appearance &amp; Device</em>, eliminating the forced <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>h-100</code> stretch class.</li><li><strong>Perfect Baseline Symmetry:</strong> On standard desktop viewports (1440px / 1920px), both columns now finish at an identical baseline height of ~1,350px. The left column''s ''Save Profile Changes'' action and the right column''s Data Privacy Act compliance banner align symmetrically with zero dead space.</li></ul><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-patch-check-fill text-accent me-2''></i>4. Automated Verification &amp; Test Suite Coverage</h5><p>To verify that all enhancements operate without regression, we authored <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>tests/test-profile-resume.php</code>, covering database column existence, user hydration aliasing, profile resume updates, access control authorization, and application auto-linking fallback rules—with <strong>12 out of 12 assertions passing</strong>. Furthermore, our complete runtime validation suite (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>tools/test-runtime-pages.php</code>) verified all 32 core system pages with <strong>0 warnings and 0 errors</strong>.</p>","key_takeaways":["Added resume_file column to student_profiles with automated DatastoreManager runtime schema checks and migrate.php bindings.","Enabled automated profile resume linking on job applications when leaving the upload input empty, eliminating repetitive file submissions.","Built dedicated Stored Profile Resume management card in settings with live preview, replacement upload, and removal actions.","Engineered ApplicationService::getStudentPlacementSummary() to detect existing campus appointments and cross-department submissions.","Implemented atomic auto_withdraw_other_applications() cascade, instantly retracting concurrent applications when a candidate is hired.","Eliminated over 1,000px of right-column dead space in settings.php, achieving clean 1:1 desktop column baseline alignment.","Validated end-to-end functionality with 12/12 passing tests in test-profile-resume.php and all 32 runtime pages verified."],"tech_stack":["PHP 8.2 & PDO MySQL","Runtime Schema Migration","Application Lifecycle State Machine","Concurrent Hiring Safeguards","Automated Withdrawal Cascade","Bootstrap 5.3 Modular Grid","UI/UX Pro Max Ergonomics"]}','2026-10-04 12:00:00'); upgraded authentication to native <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>password_hash()</code> and scrubbed hashes from session superglobals; implemented strict <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>finfo_file</code> MIME inspection on all document uploads; and scoped employer review endpoints strictly to primary-key ownership (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>employer_id === user[''id'']</code>) to eradicate IDOR vulnerabilities.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-database-check text-accent me-2''></i>Demo & Real Data Coexistence</h5><p>I removed artificial dataset switching and destructive table wipes. Demo benchmark listings and live registered student/employer accounts now coexist permanently in MySQL, with live admin COR/ID verification inspection modals in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>admin/users.php</code> that sync immediately to active sessions.</p>","key_takeaways":["Defined explicit relational foreign key constraints and UNIQUE (job_id, student_id) indexes.","Hardened authentication, file upload MIME validation, anti-CSRF tokens, and security headers.","Enforced strict IDOR primary-key ownership checks across employer review endpoints.","Enabled permanent coexistence of demo fixtures and real registered user records."],"tech_stack":["MySQL InnoDB Constraints","Bcrypt Hashing","MIME Validation (finfo)","Anti-CSRF Tokens","Defensive HTTP Headers"]}','2026-09-02 12:00:00'),('day-07','07','The 3-Step Persona Registration Wizard, Defensive Data Gating & 3D Robot Mascot Genesis','September 04, 2026','Transformed registration into an intuitive 3-step persona wizard, hardened client/server validation against double-encoding and race conditions, and integrated the 3D WebGL robot mascot with real-time cursor kinematics.','{"id":"day-07","sprint_number":"07","sprint_badge":"DAY 07 · PERSONA WIZARD & 3D MASCOT GENESIS","title":"The 3-Step Persona Registration Wizard, Defensive Data Gating & 3D Robot Mascot Genesis","date":"September 04, 2026","read_time":"6 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Transformed registration into an intuitive 3-step persona wizard, hardened client/server validation against double-encoding and race conditions, and integrated the 3D WebGL robot mascot with real-time cursor kinematics.","tags":["3-Step Wizard","Three.js WebGL","Defensive Hardening","Ocular Tracking"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-07.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>September 04 was a high-output development day spanning user onboarding UX, defensive server-side fixes, and the birth of our 3D WebGL mascot.</p><p>I completely restructured <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>register.php</code> from a long, exhausting form into an intuitive <strong>3-Step Registration Wizard</strong>. I replaced cumbersome dropdowns with a 1-click 3-persona card grid (Student Applicant, University Department, Accredited Industry Partner), an active vertical step indicator, and an 8px luminous green progress bar.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-shield-shaded text-accent me-2''></i>Relentless Defensive Hardening Marathon</h5><p>I eliminated premature <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>htmlspecialchars()</code> entity escaping across candidate evaluation notes, student cover letters, and category names, storing raw data cleanly in MySQL and preventing double-encoding (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>&amp;amp;</code>). I attached double-submission button locking with spinners across all POST forms and upgraded the student application tracker with structured status callouts and dual digital/printable CV action buttons.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-robot text-accent me-2''></i>Interactive 3D WebGL Mascot Genesis</h5><p>To give our institution a modern, friendly identity, I integrated Three.js and loaded <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>cute_robot.glb</code> into our landing hero. I isolated the primary mascot mesh, styled materials in KLD deep forest green and glowing emerald visor emission (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>#22c55e</code>), and implemented real-time cursor tracking with clamped kinematics (0.058 lerp) and dual-layer ocular visor tracking (0.10 lerp).</p>","key_takeaways":["Converted registration into a 3-step wizard with persona cards and sticky input validation.","Eliminated HTML entity double-escaping and implemented double-submit locking across all forms.","Enhanced student application tracker with structured status callouts and printable CV actions.","Integrated interactive 3D WebGL robot mascot with real-time cursor tracking and ocular visor physics."],"tech_stack":["Three.js GLTFLoader","Lerp Kinematics","Bootstrap 5 Stepper","Input Normalization","WebGL Power Optimization"]}','2026-09-03 12:00:00'),('day-08','08','Giving Life to the Mascot: 13 Kinetic Animations, Typewriter Speech Bubble & Interactive Dialogue Modes','September 05, 2026','Elevated the 3D robot mascot with 13 expressive procedural animations, synchronized head and visor micro-motions, an interactive typewriter speech bubble, and dynamic dialogue modes (/boost, /grill-me, and Talk).','{"id":"day-08","sprint_number":"08","sprint_badge":"DAY 08 · ROBOT KINEMATICS & EXPRESSIONS","title":"Giving Life to the Mascot: 13 Kinetic Animations, Typewriter Speech Bubble & Interactive Dialogue Modes","date":"September 05, 2026","read_time":"5 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Elevated the 3D robot mascot with 13 expressive procedural animations, synchronized head and visor micro-motions, an interactive typewriter speech bubble, and dynamic dialogue modes (/boost, /grill-me, and Talk).","tags":["Three.js Kinematics","3D Mascot","Procedural Motion","OLED Eye Shaders"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-08.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>Having established the 3D WebGL canvas yesterday, today''s mission was giving our robot companion true personality, charisma, and emotional depth.</p><p>I replaced basic jumping bounces with an arsenal of <strong>13 distinct procedural animations</strong> in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>assets/js/hero-robot.js</code>: winking, squinting scans, curious head tilts, excited nodding, 360° celebratory spins, empathetic sways, and respectful campus bows. Every movement is smoothly interpolated through spring-damped matrices to prevent mechanical abruptness.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-chat-quote-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Interactive Speech Bubble & Typewriter Micro-Gestures</h5><p>I engineered an interactive floating speech bubble positioned directly above the companion. As dialogue renders character-by-character via a typewriter cadence, the robot''s head and visor perform synchronized micro-bobs, giving the unmistakable impression of genuine verbal articulation.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-sliders text-accent me-2''></i>Three Dialogue Modes & OLED Visor Color Shifts</h5><p>I programmed 3 distinct interaction modes: <strong>Talk</strong> (friendly campus advice), <strong>/boost</strong> (career confidence & academic motivation), and <strong>/grill-me</strong> (rigorous mock interview preparation). When students switch modes, the companion''s OLED eye shader smoothly shifts colors—from KLD emerald green to alert amber and sharp cyan—providing immediate visual feedback.</p>","key_takeaways":["Programmed 13 procedural kinetic animations with spring damping and clamped kinematics.","Built dynamic typewriter speech bubble with synchronized mascot micro-gestures.","Implemented 3 interactive dialogue modes with real-time OLED emissive eye shader color transitions.","Optimized WebGL rendering loops with IntersectionObserver to conserve client device resources."],"tech_stack":["Three.js WebGL","Procedural Kinematics","Typewriter DOM Engine","Emissive Visor Shaders","IntersectionObserver"]}','2026-09-04 12:00:00'),('day-09','09','Integrating NVIDIA NIM AI Campus Studio: 2-Column Interface, Domain Photography & Zero-Reload Filtering','September 06, 2026','Integrated an enterprise NVIDIA NIM AI gateway with a fullscreen 2-column studio, dynamic intent detection, high-resolution domain photography across job families, and zero-reload AJAX category filtering with scroll preservation.','{"id":"day-09","sprint_number":"09","sprint_badge":"DAY 09 · NVIDIA NIM AI & VISUAL TAXONOMY","title":"Integrating NVIDIA NIM AI Campus Studio: 2-Column Interface, Domain Photography & Zero-Reload Filtering","date":"September 06, 2026","read_time":"7 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Integrated an enterprise NVIDIA NIM AI gateway with a fullscreen 2-column studio, dynamic intent detection, high-resolution domain photography across job families, and zero-reload AJAX category filtering with scroll preservation.","tags":["NVIDIA NIM AI","Fullscreen Studio","Domain Photography","Zero-Reload AJAX"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-09.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>Today we bridged artificial intelligence with high-fidelity visual design, turning our platform into a cutting-edge, visually rich student career portal.</p><p>I developed our enterprise AI Assistant integration using NVIDIA NIM (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct</code>), backed by secure server-side dispatching in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>api/robot-chat.php</code> and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>includes/ai-config.php</code>. I implemented campus intent classification (career guidance, resume writing, interview prep, policy queries) and built an immersive <strong>Fullscreen 2-Column Studio</strong> that pairs our live 3D mascot on the left with a real-time markdown chat stream console on the right.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-images text-accent me-2''></i>Domain Photography & Visual Taxonomy Showcase</h5><p>To eliminate clinical corporate monotony, I upgraded our entire category taxonomy with high-resolution photography representing campus job families (Tech Lab, Library, Science Research, Peer Tutoring, Athletic Facility, Creative Media, Administrative Office, Campus Cafe). I designed glassmorphic badge overlays for verified employers, work setups, and hourly rates, and built a rich visual category showcase banner in both <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>student/jobs.php</code> and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>admin/categories.php</code>.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-arrow-repeat text-accent me-2''></i>Zero-Reload AJAX Filtering & FAQ Bot</h5><p>I upgraded job browsing so students can filter by job families without jarring full-page reloads. Using vanilla JS fetch and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>history.pushState()</code>, the DOM updates asynchronously while completely preserving scroll position. Finally, I integrated the Campus AI assistant directly into the FAQ page (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>faqs.php</code>) to answer unlisted student questions on demand.</p>","key_takeaways":["Integrated NVIDIA NIM AI gateway with intent classification, rate limiting, and local curated fallbacks.","Constructed immersive 2-column fullscreen studio uniting 3D WebGL mascot with streaming markdown chat.","Overhauled job cards and category taxonomy with domain photography and glassmorphic metadata chips.","Engineered zero-reload AJAX category filtering with HTML5 pushState history and scroll preservation."],"tech_stack":["NVIDIA NIM API","Fullscreen Studio Layout","Vanilla JS Fetch API","HTML5 History API","Glassmorphism Tokens"]}','2026-09-05 12:00:00'),('day-10','10','Building the Multi-Role Notification Engine: Real-Time Polling, Verification Triggers & Migration Whitelists','September 07, 2026','Architected an asynchronous multi-role notification pipeline with 30-second background polling, lifecycle verification triggers across student applications and employer accreditations, and hardened database migration loops with strict table whitelisting.','{"id":"day-10","sprint_number":"10","sprint_badge":"DAY 10 · REAL-TIME NOTIFICATIONS & ENGINE SECURITY","title":"Building the Multi-Role Notification Engine: Real-Time Polling, Verification Triggers & Migration Whitelists","date":"September 07, 2026","read_time":"5 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Architected an asynchronous multi-role notification pipeline with 30-second background polling, lifecycle verification triggers across student applications and employer accreditations, and hardened database migration loops with strict table whitelisting.","tags":["Notification System","AJAX Polling","Lifecycle Triggers","Migration Security"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-10.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>Clear communication and instantaneous feedback are critical for our multi-role institutional platform. Today, I built an end-to-end real-time in-app notification infrastructure.</p><p>I established the relational <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>notifications</code> table in MySQL with foreign key constraints, indexes, and automated cascading cleanup. In <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>includes/data-helper.php</code>, I implemented dynamic lifecycle event triggers: students receive instant updates when their application shifts state (Under Review, Interview Scheduled with date & venue, Accepted, Declined) and when profile change requests are resolved. Employers are alerted immediately upon new student submissions or when their institutional accreditation is verified, while admins receive real-time notifications for incoming registrations and student COR requests.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-bell-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Navbar Dropdown, Toast Alerts & Notification Center</h5><p>I engineered <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>api/notifications.php</code> and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>assets/js/notifications.js</code> to handle 30-second background polling with <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>document.visibilitychange</code> lifecycle pausing to preserve battery and network bandwidth. Unread pings display non-intrusive floating toasts and increment the navbar bell counter. Furthermore, I built a dedicated Notification Center (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>notifications.php</code>) featuring chip-filtered tabs (All/Unread), ''Mark All as Read'', and direct deep-links to associated records.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-shield-check text-accent me-2''></i>Migration Truncate Whitelist Hardening</h5><p>To eliminate any possibility of command injection or malicious table manipulation during database resets, I hardened <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>database/migrate.php</code> by wrapping all truncate operations in a strict table name whitelist array validated by regex prior to execution.</p>","key_takeaways":["Engineered relational notifications schema with user foreign keys and automated lifecycle triggers.","Built 30-second background polling engine with tab visibility suspension and floating toast alerts.","Developed comprehensive Notification Center (notifications.php) with unread filtering and batch actions.","Hardened database migration reset scripts with strict table whitelist and regex validation."],"tech_stack":["MySQL Foreign Keys","AJAX Background Polling","Lifecycle Event Hooks","Floating Toast UI","Regex Whitelisting"]}','2026-09-06 12:00:00'),('day-11','11','Modular CSS Architecture, Role-Based Navbar, Multi-Turn AI Memory & 20-Hour Academic Labor Cap','September 08, 2026','Refactored monolithic CSS into 7 scoped architectural modules, engineered dynamic role-based navbar routing with a centered Google-style spotlight search, added multi-turn conversational memory to Campus AI, and strictly capped weekly student assistant hours to 20h.','{"id":"day-11","sprint_number":"11","sprint_badge":"DAY 11 · MODULAR CSS & 20H POLICY SAFEGUARDS","title":"Modular CSS Architecture, Role-Based Navbar, Multi-Turn AI Memory & 20-Hour Academic Labor Cap","date":"September 08, 2026","read_time":"6 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Refactored monolithic CSS into 7 scoped architectural modules, engineered dynamic role-based navbar routing with a centered Google-style spotlight search, added multi-turn conversational memory to Campus AI, and strictly capped weekly student assistant hours to 20h.","tags":["Modular CSS","Role Navbar","Multi-Turn AI","20-Hour Policy","Mobile UX"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-11.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>With our final presentation and system evaluation on the horizon, today was dedicated to high-level structural refactoring, navigational fluidity, and strict institutional policy enforcement.</p><p>As systems grow in complexity, stylesheet maintenance can quickly degrade without strict discipline. I tackled this head-on today by breaking apart our monolithic <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>custom.css</code> into 7 domain-specific modules: <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>variables.css</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>base.css</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>components.css</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>layout.css</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>auth.css</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>dashboard.css</code>, and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>robot.css</code>. To optimize asset delivery, I replaced timestamp query cache-busting with <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>filemtime()</code> in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>includes/header.php</code>, ensuring optimal client caching while guaranteeing real-time updates when files are edited.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-grid-fill text-accent me-2''></i>3-Column Role Navbar & Centered Spotlight Search</h5><p>I completely restructured <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>navbar.php</code> using a clean 3-column CSS Grid. The campus brand logo now routes dynamically based on session role—sending students directly to <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>student/dashboard.php</code>, employers to their requisitions, and admins to analytical reports. For authenticated users, I introduced an elegant centered Google-style search bar that triggers our debounced universal spotlight search modal (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>Ctrl+K</code>) without layout jitter or horizontal collisions.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-chat-left-dots-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Campus AI Multi-Turn Memory & Navigation Intelligence</h5><p>I upgraded our Campus AI companion gateway by feeding the entire portal sitemap and session role context into the system prompt. Conversations now retain a sliding multi-turn conversational memory across <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>faqs.php</code> and the hero assistant, with plural-aware regex for our curated local offline fallback engine.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-clock-history text-accent me-2''></i>Institutional 20-Hour Labor Cap & Mobile Filters</h5><p>To strictly adhere to the university standard safeguarding student academic standing, I implemented client and server-side validation capping weekly student assistant shifts to a hard maximum of <strong>20 hours per week</strong> across job requisition creation and editing forms. Furthermore, I redesigned the shared footer into an unsegmented modern unit and transformed the mobile job search filters into a smooth collapsible accordion with live filter count badges.</p>","key_takeaways":["Modularized monolithic CSS into 7 scoped stylesheets and integrated filemtime() asset caching.","Engineered 3-column CSS Grid navbar with dynamic role-based logo routing and centered spotlight search.","Implemented multi-turn conversational memory and sitemap navigation in Campus AI companion.","Strictly enforced statutory 20-hour/week student labor cap with server-side validation."],"tech_stack":["Modular CSS Architecture","CSS Grid 3-Column Navbar","Multi-Turn AI Memory","Policy Validation","filemtime Caching"]}','2026-09-07 12:00:00'),('day-12','12','Tactile De-Pilling, 14-Pillar Tech Architecture Overhaul, Filter Consolidation & 3D Typography Sharpness','September 09, 2026','Enforced strict paper aesthetic guidelines by eliminating decorative pill clutter across About Us and DevBlog, overhauled Technical Architecture to showcase our authentic 14-pillar stack (Three.js WebGL & GLTF robot, MySQL/MariaDB PDO, NVIDIA NIM AI), unified redundant reset controls, and eradicated 3D perspective blur for crystal-sharp typography.','{"id":"day-12","sprint_number":"12","sprint_badge":"DAY 12 · DE-PILLING, ARCHITECTURE & GPU RENDERING","title":"Tactile De-Pilling, 14-Pillar Tech Architecture Overhaul, Filter Consolidation & 3D Typography Sharpness","date":"September 09, 2026","read_time":"7 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Enforced strict paper aesthetic guidelines by eliminating decorative pill clutter across About Us and DevBlog, overhauled Technical Architecture to showcase our authentic 14-pillar stack (Three.js WebGL & GLTF robot, MySQL/MariaDB PDO, NVIDIA NIM AI), unified redundant reset controls, and eradicated 3D perspective blur for crystal-sharp typography.","tags":["Tactile Paper UI","Three.js & GLTF","14-Pillar Stack","Filter Consolidation","GPU Subpixel Sharpness"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-12.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>Today was a milestone in design purity, architectural transparency, and rendering precision. We eliminated decorative pill clutter, brought our technical documentation in line with our real 14-pillar engineering stack, unified student filter controls, and diagnosed and cured GPU texture magnification blur across our 3D stage.</p><p>As our project evolved, visual debt accumulated in the form of decorative rounded pill badges and stadium capsules that violated our tactile Paper Sheet aesthetic guidelines. I led a comprehensive cleanup across <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>about-us.php</code>, stripping away decorative eyebrow tags and transforming card badges, author date tags, developer role badges, and navigation controls into crisp, structured paper chips with subtle borders and intentional typography. In the interactive reader modal, I removed the redundant bottom close button and footer entirely, reclaiming prime reading space for engineering narratives and deliverables.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-cpu-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Overhauling Technical Architecture: The Authentic 14 Pillars</h5><p>Our About Us page had previously displayed legacy placeholder notes referencing a flat-file JSON datastore. I completely replaced that section with an authentic <strong>14-Pillar Technical Architecture Spec Grid</strong> (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>.tech-spec-grid</code>). It transparently details our full production stack: <strong>Three.js WebGL & GLTFLoader</strong> driving our 3D robot mascot (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>cute_robot.glb</code>) with 13 procedural kinematics and OLED visor shaders, <strong>MySQL 8.0/MariaDB (InnoDB)</strong> with ACID transactions, <strong>PHP PDO Prepared Statements</strong> with zero SQL injection vectors, atomic database migrations (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>database/migrate.php</code>), Native PHP 8.2+ RBAC, NVIDIA NIM AI Gateway (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct</code>) with multi-turn memory, local heuristic fallbacks, modular CSS design tokens, Bootstrap 5.3, vanilla ES6+ JavaScript with Shannon entropy calculations, 30s background notification polling, Bcrypt/anti-CSRF security, and our 26-spec Playwright E2E automation suite.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-funnel-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Student Jobs: Filter Consolidation & Category Data Integrity</h5><p>On <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>student/jobs.php</code>, three competing reset controls previously crowded the viewport (hero banner reset pill, category header clear link, and toolbar reset button). I consolidated these down to a single authoritative reset button in the filter toolbar and replaced the hero pill with an informative Active Discipline badge. Concurrently, I tracked down an insidious category count bug in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>includes/data-helper.php</code> where categories without active jobs retained static seed numbers; I fixed the aggregation fallback and seeded the missing Sports & Athletics Aide jobs (#9 and #10) so the live catalog perfectly matches database records.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-eye-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Diagnosing & Eradicating 3D GPU Perspective Blur</h5><p>When inspecting our 3D Coverflow DevBlog, we noticed a subtle rendering flaw: text on the front active card appeared fuzzy and blurry, while cards in the back remained sharp. Profiling Chromium''s rendering pipeline revealed that <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>translateZ(80px)</code> under <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>perspective: 1400px</code> projected the front card 6% closer to the camera, forcing the GPU to stretch the 1x offscreen bitmap texture bilinearly instead of re-rasterizing vector glyphs. Meanwhile, back cards were scaled down (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>scale(0.86)</code>), downsampling pixels crisply. Furthermore, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>transform-style: preserve-3d</code> ignored DOM z-index, causing rotated side cards to slice through flat elements. I eliminated <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>translateZ(80px)</code>, switched the track to <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>transform-style: flat</code>, and applied individual perspective to flanking cards. The active card now renders at exact 1:1 pixel scale with razor-sharp subpixel ClearType antialiasing and flawless z-index stacking!</p>","key_takeaways":["Enforced tactile paper design guidelines by de-pilling About Us and DevBlog, removing duplicate modal footer.","Overhauled Technical Architecture to showcase authentic 14-pillar stack featuring Three.js, MySQL PDO, and NVIDIA NIM.","Consolidated 3 redundant filter reset controls on student jobs and resolved category count aggregation bug.","Eliminated 3D GPU perspective texture magnification blur, restoring razor-sharp 1:1 subpixel typography on the active card."],"tech_stack":["Three.js WebGL","MySQL InnoDB","CSS 3D Projection Optimization","Subpixel Typography","UI/UX Paper Tokens","Playwright E2E"]}','2026-09-08 12:00:00'),('day-13','13','Dual-Persona Developer Photography, Cyber Glitch & RGB Split Transitions, Unified Chatbot Modal & Global Dark Overrides','September 10, 2026','Engineered dynamic dual-persona developer photography with light/dark portraits across all team touchpoints, crafted a 300ms hardware-accelerated Cyber Glitch & RGB Split transition with Hover Peek preview, unified the FAQ Chatbot with the index 3D robot companion modal, and resolved global dark mode contrast anomalies.','{"id":"day-13","sprint_number":"13","sprint_badge":"DAY 13 · DUAL PERSONAS & CYBER GLITCH ENGINE","title":"Dual-Persona Developer Photography, Cyber Glitch & RGB Split Transitions, Unified Chatbot Modal & Global Dark Overrides","date":"September 10, 2026","read_time":"7 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Engineered dynamic dual-persona developer photography with light/dark portraits across all team touchpoints, crafted a 300ms hardware-accelerated Cyber Glitch & RGB Split transition with Hover Peek preview, unified the FAQ Chatbot with the index 3D robot companion modal, and resolved global dark mode contrast anomalies.","tags":["Dual-Persona Photos","Cyber Glitch Transition","RGB Split FX","Hover Peek","Unified Chatbot Modal","Dark Mode Polish"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-13.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>Today brought our system''s visual identity, responsiveness, and interactive polish to an unprecedented level. We engineered dynamic dual-persona developer photography with custom Cyber Glitch and RGB Split transitions, unified our Campus AI assistant modal across pages, and resolved complex dark mode contrast edge cases.</p><p>As part of our mission to deliver a world-class institutional experience, our team needed to embody the dual character of our platform: clean, crisp institutional day-to-day operations in daytime mode, and high-performance engineering focus in dark mode. We introduced formal dual-persona 2x2 institutional portraits for all six developers—featuring daytime institutional attire and sleek dark mode photography across the About Us team grid, the DevBlog coverflow, and the floating landing page circles.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-lightning-charge-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Cyber Glitch & RGB Split Transition Engine</h5><p>Rather than settling for a standard opacity fade when toggling themes, I designed and coded a custom, hardware-accelerated <strong>Cyber Glitch & RGB Split Transition</strong>. Built using CSS3 <code>drop-shadow</code> chromatic aberration (splitting into cyan <code>#00F0FF</code> and neon crimson <code>#FF1E56</code> channels), horizontal slice jitter (<code>skewX</code> and subpixel displacements), and an animated scanline sweep, the 320ms transition delivers a tactile, sci-fi cyberpunk feel without any audio intrusion or performance hitching.</p><p>To eliminate any perceptual latency or white flicker during rapid toggling, the engine runs an asset preloading cycle on DOM ready, caching both light and dark portraits in browser memory. The image source swap executes at the exact 140ms midpoint peak of maximum jitter distortion, ensuring a seamless visual transformation. Furthermore, I engineered an interactive <strong>Hover Peek</strong> capability: hovering over any developer card or floating bubble triggers a micro-glitch preview revealing the alternate persona, smoothly restoring when the cursor leaves.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-robot text-accent me-2''></i>Unified Campus AI Assistant Modal</h5><p>On <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>faqs.php</code>, the chatbot previously rendered as an isolated offcanvas drawer that conflicted with our paper design language. Today, I completely unified the FAQ chatbot interface with our flagship full-screen 2-column modal from the index page. Powered by our Three.js 3D GLTF robot companion and NVIDIA NIM AI Cloud Gateway, the unified assistant modal delivers full multi-turn conversational intelligence, instant topic suggestions, and zero-reload responsiveness across the portal.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-moon-stars-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Dark Mode Typography & Contrast Hardening</h5><p>We audited all interface surfaces in dark mode, curing contrast regressions across badge indicators, numeric counters, form inputs, call-to-action buttons, and calendar icons. Buttons such as the index CTA now boast high-contrast dark text on bright KLD Green, and secondary buttons feature clear luminous borders and crisp icons. Our automated Playwright suite confirmed 100% test success with zero regressions across both light and dark themes!</p>","key_takeaways":["Engineered dual-persona developer photography with light and dark portraits across all team touchpoints.","Created 300ms hardware-accelerated Cyber Glitch & RGB Split transition with instant preloading and Hover Peek preview.","Unified FAQ chatbot with the index 3D robot companion modal for a seamless multi-turn AI experience.","Hardened global dark mode styling, curing contrast anomalies across badges, counters, and action buttons."],"tech_stack":["CSS3 Chromatic Aberration","Hardware-Accelerated Glitch","Vanilla JS Theme Engine","Dual-Persona Photography","Three.js Robot Companion","Playwright E2E Suite"]}','2026-09-09 12:00:00'),('day-14','14','Sealing Demo Backdoors, Unifying Table Flags & Shipping the Accepted-Student Flow','September 11, 2026','Gated the passwordless demo hooks to loopback-only, fixed an Apply redirect that silently signed guests in as another student, replaced rainbow table pills with a uniform dot-flag system, cut the job-card photo to a single overlay, and shipped an opt-in withdraw-others flow for accepted students — every change proven with curl traces and Playwright screenshots.','{"id":"day-14","sprint_number":"14","sprint_badge":"DAY 14 · TRUST HARDENING & PAPER DISCIPLINE","title":"Sealing Demo Backdoors, Unifying Table Flags & Shipping the Accepted-Student Flow","date":"September 11, 2026","read_time":"8 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Gated the passwordless demo hooks to loopback-only, fixed an Apply redirect that silently signed guests in as another student, replaced rainbow table pills with a uniform dot-flag system, cut the job-card photo to a single overlay, and shipped an opt-in withdraw-others flow for accepted students — every change proven with curl traces and Playwright screenshots.","tags":["Demo Backdoor Gating","Return-To Auth","Cell-Flag System","Accept Flow","De-Pilling","Playwright Proof"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-14.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>September 11 was a trust-and-clarity sprint: every path that could silently sign a visitor in as someone else got sealed, tables and cards were stripped of pill clutter, and accepted students finally got a dignified way to release their other pending applications — each change proven with curl traces and Playwright screenshots.</p><p>A production audit with fresh eyes surfaced an uncomfortable truth: our beloved demo conveniences had leaked into user-facing flows. The E2E reset and passwordless login hooks in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>login.php</code> answered to anyone who asked, and worse, the guest Apply redirect pointed at <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>login.php?demo=student</code> — so a visitor who clicked Apply Now on the homepage woke up signed in as Juan Dela Cruz. I gated both hooks to loopback-only plus a non-production <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>APP_ENV</code> with a strict student/employer/admin role whitelist, and rerouted guests to the plain login form carrying a whitelisted <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>next</code> return-to target (relative portal paths only — an evil.com payload was curl-tested and rejected). After a manual sign-in, students land back on the exact requisition they wanted.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-palette-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Paper Discipline: Pills, Emojis & Phantom Domains</h5><p>The shared <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>render_page_head()</code> helper defaulted every page title to a green badge pill, in direct violation of our own badges-for-data-only law — it now emits a plain-text kicker, and the homepage and forgot-password pills followed it into eyebrow text. All eight category preset emojis (duplicated across both admin modals) became proper Bootstrap icons, all twelve Campus AI reply templates were de-emojied with the JSON API contract returned to plain text, and six stray <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>campus-hire.edu</code> contacts were unified to the real <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>kld.edu.ph</code> domain. The CAMPUS FAQ badge and its siblings (AI Companion, Student Career Copilot) were purged from both fullscreen chatbot modals and the speech bubble, the redundant green dark-mode switch in Settings was deleted in favor of the segmented control, and the duplicate Back to Vacancies button on job details was removed.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-table text-accent me-2''></i>Tables: One Box, One Dot</h5><p>The analytics table swapped pill classes per cell value, so IN PROGRESS rendered visibly larger than Open Quota and a 1/5 fill count looked nothing like its 0/6 neighbors. The new <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>.cell-flag</code> system gives every state one identical 28px box — ink text, hairline border — with meaning carried only by a 7px status dot (filled, in-progress, over-quota, open), all tokens carrying dark-mode values. Fill counts are now permanently neutral chips since the ratio bar and the flag already tell the story, the decorative Term pill became plain text, and the job-card photo dropped from four overlay pills to a single Featured ribbon with employer type, category, and pay relocated to a clean body metadata row.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-check-circle-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Accepted-Student Flow: Prompt, Never Force</h5><p>No auto-withdraw existed — accepting a student only bumped slot counters and sent a notification. I deliberately chose prompt-to-withdraw over silent auto-withdraw: students may legitimately stack OJT with part-time work, and silent deletes invite RA 10173 disputes and confused supervisors. A CSRF-guarded <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>withdraw_others</code> handler (pending-only, ownership-checked, confirm-guarded) powers a congratulations banner that persists across logins until the record is clean. I staged a demo Juan with one acceptance and two pending applications, captured the screenshots, then deleted the demo rows and reverted — with the database verified byte-identical to its prior state.</p>","key_takeaways":["Gated ?reset/?demo hooks to loopback + non-production with role whitelisting, and fixed a guest Apply redirect that auto-logged visitors in as another student.","Shipped a whitelisted next return-to flow so guests land back on their exact requisition after a manual sign-in, with open redirects curl-tested shut.","Replaced per-value table pills with a uniform .cell-flag dot system and cut job-card photos to a single Featured overlay.","Built an opt-in withdraw-others flow for accepted students with CSRF + ownership guards, proven via Playwright screenshots with full demo-data cleanup."],"tech_stack":["Loopback-Gated Test Hooks","Open-Redirect Whitelisting","CSS Status Tokens","Paper Dot Flags","CSRF-Guarded Mutations","Playwright E2E Screenshots"]}','2026-09-10 12:00:00'),('day-15','15','Option C Relational Overhaul: Strict 3NF Decomposition, Pure Junction Tables & Multi-Tier Verification','September 12, 2026','Decomposed the polymorphic users table into clean 3NF with Class Table Inheritance, converted applications into a pure junction table with relational hydration, fixed a subtle MySQL left-to-right SET evaluation bug in vacancy auto-closure, enforced concurrency quota ceilings with SELECT FOR UPDATE, and verified 201/201 multi-tier test assertions via Bun and Playwright.','{"id":"day-15","sprint_number":"15","sprint_badge":"DAY 15 · 3NF ARCHITECTURE & ADVERSARIAL CERTIFICATION","title":"Option C Relational Overhaul: Strict 3NF Decomposition, Pure Junction Tables & Multi-Tier Verification","date":"September 12, 2026","read_time":"8 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Decomposed the polymorphic users table into clean 3NF with Class Table Inheritance, converted applications into a pure junction table with relational hydration, fixed a subtle MySQL left-to-right SET evaluation bug in vacancy auto-closure, enforced concurrency quota ceilings with SELECT FOR UPDATE, and verified 201/201 multi-tier test assertions via Bun and Playwright.","tags":["3NF Normalization","Class Table Inheritance","Junction Tables","Concurrency Locking","Adversarial Testing","Bun & Playwright","De-Pilling"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-15.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>September 12 was our most significant data architecture and reliability sprint to date. We committed to Option C: full Third Normal Form (3NF) relational refactoring with Class Table Inheritance, purged all denormalized snapshots, resolved insidious concurrency edge cases in vacancy auto-closure, and certified the entire system across 201 automated test assertions powered by Bun and Playwright.</p><p>Our database had historically relied on a wide, polymorphic <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>users</code> table packed with mutually exclusive nullable columns for student program and course records and employer office accreditation. Today, we dismantled that flat design. We decomposed identity into a pure authentication supertype <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>users</code> and two dedicated 1-to-1 subtype profile tables: <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>student_profiles</code> and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>employer_profiles</code>, sharing primary keys with cascading referential actions. Simultaneously, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>applications</code> was stripped of duplicated snapshot fields (such as student names, contacts, and job titles), transforming it into a lean, pure 3NF junction table governed by a compound <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>UNIQUE(job_id, student_id)</code> constraint.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-layers-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Zero-Downtime Backward Compatibility via Hydration</h5><p>Refactoring core database tables can easily break presentation layers across student, employer, and administrative views. To achieve zero regressions without modifying dozens of front-end templates, we engineered a sophisticated relational hydration layer in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>includes/data-helper.php</code>. Functions like <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>get_user_base_query()</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>hydrate_user()</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>hydrate_job()</code>, and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>hydrate_application()</code> dynamically execute optimized SQL joins at query time to synthesize all expected attributes on the fly with zero PHP notices or warnings.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-bug-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Adversarial Auditing: Catching the Left-to-Right SET Bug</h5><p>During our adversarial stress audit, our test harness uncovered a subtle, critical defect in vacancy auto-closure. In MySQL, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>UPDATE ... SET</code> clauses are evaluated left to right. Because <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>slots_filled = slots_filled + 1</code> executed first, the subsequent CASE condition checking <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>slots_filled + 1 >= slots_total</code> was reading the <em>already-incremented</em> value! This resulted in premature auto-closure after only N-1 candidates were accepted. We eliminated the redundant increment in the CASE condition and wrapped applicant acceptance in a pessimistic <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>SELECT ... FOR UPDATE</code> lock to strictly enforce vacancy capacity ceilings against concurrent acceptances.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-speedometer2 text-accent me-2''></i>Fast Multi-Tier Verification with Bun & Playwright</h5><p>To verify that our refactored relational foundation is rock-solid, we migrated our test runner execution to <strong>Bun</strong> for sub-second tooling startup. We ran our comprehensive dual integration suite (61/61 passed), the adversarial edge case audit (29/29 passed), the lifecycle notifications suite, and all 8 Playwright browser automation suites across desktop, half-screen (680px-960px), and mobile viewports. The outcome was definitive: <strong>201 out of 201 automated test assertions passed cleanly</strong> with zero database constraint violations and zero console errors.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-brush text-accent me-2''></i>Strict UI Clean UI & Typography Enforcement</h5><p>We also performed a final pass on UI cleanliness, removing legacy decorative badge pills and eyebrow tags above headings in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>admin/categories.php</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>admin/updates.php</code>, and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>update-detail.php</code>. In strict compliance with our UI guidelines, headings now stand with clean typographic hierarchy, reserving badges strictly for dynamic application workflow states and notification counters.</p>","key_takeaways":["Refactored database to strict 3NF with Class Table Inheritance (users, student_profiles, employer_profiles).","Converted applications to a pure 3NF junction table with dynamic SQL hydration and compound uniqueness.","Patched MySQL left-to-right SET evaluation flaw in vacancy auto-closure and added SELECT FOR UPDATE ceiling locks.","Hardened registration role tampering, unscoped selectors, and eliminated decorative pill clutter above headings.","Achieved 100% pass rate across all 201 multi-tier test assertions (111 Playwright + 61 integration + 29 adversarial) via Bun."],"tech_stack":["Third Normal Form (3NF)","Class Table Inheritance (CTI)","Pessimistic Locking (FOR UPDATE)","MySQL 8 InnoDB FKs","Bun Runtime","Playwright E2E Suite","Tactile UI Typography & Tokens"]}','2026-09-11 12:00:00'),('day-16','16','Dual-Factor Trust: 6-Digit Institutional Email Verification, Password Reset Engine & In-Card Celebration Morph','September 20, 2026','Engineered cryptographically secure 6-digit institutional email verification and self-service password reset flows with PHPMailer SMTP, built tactile monospace digit pods with haptic shake and a 1.2s in-card SVG success morph, resolved foreign key cascade edge cases on resend, and preserved evaluation demo readiness via backward-compatible schema migration.','{"id":"day-16","sprint_number":"16","sprint_badge":"DAY 16 · INSTITUTIONAL OTP VERIFICATION & TACTILE AUTH","title":"Dual-Factor Trust: 6-Digit Institutional Email Verification, Password Reset Engine & In-Card Celebration Morph","date":"September 20, 2026","read_time":"9 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Engineered cryptographically secure 6-digit institutional email verification and self-service password reset flows with PHPMailer SMTP, built tactile monospace digit pods with haptic shake and a 1.2s in-card SVG success morph, resolved foreign key cascade edge cases on resend, and preserved evaluation demo readiness via backward-compatible schema migration.","tags":["Email Verification","6-Digit OTP","PHPMailer SMTP","Password Reset","Tactile Pods UI","SVG Checkmark Animation","Schema Migration","FK Cascades"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-16.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>September 20 marked our transition from open self-attested identity to strict institutional cryptographic verification. We implemented end-to-end 6-digit email OTP verification and self-service password reset engines powered by PHPMailer, designed custom monospace digit pods with haptic error recoil and in-card SVG celebration morphs, resolved critical foreign key cascade edge cases on resend, and ensured seamless backward compatibility for existing evaluation accounts.</p><p>As our campus job ecosystem prepares for formal institutional deployment, self-attested registration posed an undeniable security vector: anyone could register arbitrary student or employer emails without proving ownership of the institutional inbox. Today, we closed that loop completely. Every new registration across student and employer personas is now strictly staged in an unverified state until the user proves inbox control via an ephemeral, single-use 6-digit passcode.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-shield-lock-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Cryptographic OTP Engine &amp; State Machine</h5><p>Rather than storing raw passcodes or relying on transient session variables, we architected a dedicated relational verification ledger in MySQL: <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>email_verifications</code>. Passcodes are generated via cryptographically secure pseudo-random integers (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>random_int(100000, 999999)</code>) and hashed using SHA-256 before disk persistence. The ledger enforces strict defense-in-depth policies: a 15-minute validity window, an automated 5-attempt brute-force lockout, and a 60-second resend cooldown timer. Upon successful validation, the user record seamlessly graduates to <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>is_email_verified = 1</code> and active session authorization.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-envelope-check-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Transactional Outbound Mail Delivery via PHPMailer</h5><p>We engineered a modular outbound email transport layer in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>includes/mailer.php</code> leveraging PHPMailer. Configured through environment variables (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>MAIL_HOST</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>MAIL_PORT</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>MAIL_USERNAME</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>MAIL_PASSWORD</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>MAIL_ENCRYPTION</code>), the transport supports authenticated TLS/STARTTLS delivery to institutional mail servers and Google Workspace. For developer environments without active credentials, the engine fails gracefully with clear UI notices, preventing thread hangs or fatal exceptions.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-palette-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Tactile Monospace Pods, Haptic Shake &amp; In-Card Celebration Morph</h5><p>Standard full-width inputs feel cold and clunky for one-time passcodes. We crafted a dedicated 6-digit UI component in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>verify-email.php</code> and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>assets/js/otp-verify.js</code>. Six fixed-dimension <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>52px × 62px</code> pods render with bold 28px monospace typography, responsive across desktop and mobile screens. The interface supports single-digit typing with auto-advance, intelligent backspace navigation, arrow traversal, and instant 6-digit clipboard paste parsing. On invalid submissions, the container triggers a crisp haptic shake animation (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>@keyframes otpShake</code>), resets the pods, and refocuses digit zero. On correct entry, the pods illuminate in emerald, the card smoothly morphs, and an SVG checkmark dynamically draws along its path (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>stroke-dashoffset</code>) above an emerald progress bar before redirecting to the student or employer dashboard.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-database-check text-accent me-2''></i>Foreign Key Hardening &amp; Evaluation Account Continuity</h5><p>During adversarial manual testing, we caught and patched a subtle edge case: if an unverified user was purged from <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>users</code> while their browser session remained open, clicking Resend Code triggered a MySQL 1452 foreign key integrity violation. We hardened all helper methods to verify referential existence before query dispatch, gracefully invalidating stale sessions and redirecting to login. Finally, we preserved evaluation account readiness: the schema migration initialized existing pre-seeded evaluation accounts with verified status, ensuring demo reviewers and thesis panelists can inspect candidate profiles and employer dashboards without friction.</p>","key_takeaways":["Implemented cryptographically secure 6-digit institutional email verification with SHA-256 token hashing, 15-minute expiry, and 5-attempt lockout.","Engineered transactional email dispatch via PHPMailer supporting TLS SMTP delivery and graceful unconfigured fallbacks.","Created custom 52px × 62px monospace digit pods with auto-advance, full clipboard paste parsing, and haptic shake on rejection.","Crafted a 1.2-second in-card success celebration featuring an animated SVG drawing checkmark and emerald progress redirect bar.","Hardened MySQL foreign key cascades on resend to eliminate orphaned session errors, preserving evaluation demo accounts."],"tech_stack":["PHPMailer 6.9","SHA-256 Passcode Hashing","MySQL InnoDB FK Cascades","Monospace Pods UI","CSS Keyframes & SVG Stroke Dashoffset","Vanilla ES6 Fetch & Clipboard API"]}','2026-09-19 12:00:00'),('day-17','17','Defense-in-Depth Hardening: Live DNS MX Resolution, Dual-Layer Password Entropy & TypeSafe Clean Architecture Certification','September 21, 2026','Hardened institutional authentication with live DNS MX/A domain verification before transactional mail dispatch, eliminated insecure password reset vulnerability via dual-layer complexity validation and real-time entropy scoring, and certified clean architecture (0.8600) under TypeSafe System One quality gates.','{"id":"day-17","sprint_number":"17","sprint_badge":"DAY 17 · PASSWORD ENTROPY & DNS DOMAIN HARDENING","title":"Defense-in-Depth Hardening: Live DNS MX Resolution, Dual-Layer Password Entropy & TypeSafe Clean Architecture Certification","date":"September 21, 2026","read_time":"8 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Hardened institutional authentication with live DNS MX/A domain verification before transactional mail dispatch, eliminated insecure password reset vulnerability via dual-layer complexity validation and real-time entropy scoring, and certified clean architecture (0.8600) under TypeSafe System One quality gates.","tags":["Password Entropy","DNS MX Verification","Account Recovery","Real-Time Validation","Clean Architecture","TypeSafe System One","Jev Quality Gate","Security Hardening"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-17.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>September 21 was dedicated to closing critical security boundaries in identity lifecycle management. We engineered live DNS MX record verification to prevent phantom outbound email dispatch, eliminated a critical vulnerability in account recovery where arbitrary passwords could be set during reset, unified our client-side real-time Shannon entropy engine across registration and recovery flows, and certified our implementation against TypeSafe System One (Jev) automated clean architecture quality gates.</p><p>While yesterday''s implementation of 6-digit cryptographic email verification established provable inbox ownership, thorough adversarial probing revealed two subtle yet critical security vectors in the authentication lifecycle: first, users could request reset tokens or register with syntactically valid yet non-existent domain names (causing unnecessary SMTP timeouts and delivery failures); second, our password reset endpoint permitted arbitrary passwords without the strict multi-class entropy checks enforced during registration.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-globe-americas text-accent me-2''></i>Live DNS MX &amp; Subdomain Verification Before SMTP Dispatch</h5><p>To eliminate wasted transactional mail attempts and defend against garbage email registrations, we engineered <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>validate_email_domain_dns($email)</code> in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>includes/data-helper.php</code>. Beyond basic regex formatting, the engine extracts the host domain, performs low-level DNS MX record lookups via <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>checkdnsrr($domain, ''MX'')</code>, and falls back to address record validation (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>checkdnsrr($domain, ''A'')</code>). Requests to bogus or dead domains are now rejected immediately at the input layer before contacting the PHPMailer transport layer.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-shield-lock-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Dual-Layer Password Complexity &amp; Real-Time Entropy Scoring</h5><p>We addressed the account recovery security flaw where users could bypass password strength recommendations. We architected a shared server-side validator, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>validate_password_strength($password)</code>, enforcing an 8-character minimum ceiling and requiring at least two distinct character classes (lowercase, uppercase, numbers, symbols). Simultaneously, we extended our standalone JavaScript entropy analyzer (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>assets/js/password-strength.js</code>) to dynamically bind to the password reset form (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>#reset-password-form</code>), providing real-time visual meter fill transitions, textual strength feedback, and client-side submission blocking for weak inputs.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-patch-check-fill text-accent me-2''></i>TypeSafe System One (Jev) Clean Architecture Certification</h5><p>In accordance with our strict engineering quality directives, all refactored authentication controllers and UI scripts were evaluated against the TypeSafe System One (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>jev-gate</code>) automated quality gate. By eliminating redundant wrapper abstractions, avoiding inline handler slop, and preserving idiomatic PHP and vanilla JavaScript paradigms, our final staged changeset achieved a clean architecture rating of <strong class=''text-accent''>0.8600</strong> (exceeding the 0.8500 gate threshold), certifying production readiness ahead of formal institutional defense.</p>","key_takeaways":["Implemented live DNS MX and A record domain validation to reject phantom emails prior to SMTP dispatch.","Closed forgot-password security gap by enforcing dual-layer password complexity (8+ chars, 2+ character classes).","Unified real-time client-side Shannon password entropy analyzer across registration and reset workflows.","Certified clean architecture under TypeSafe System One (jev-gate) with a 0.8600 quality gate score.","Guaranteed single-use reset token invalidation upon password consumption, protecting against token replay attacks."],"tech_stack":["Native PHP 8.2","DNS MX/A Verification","Shannon Password Entropy","TypeSafe System One (Jev 1.13)","Vanilla ES6 DOM","CSS Custom Properties & Transitions"]}','2026-09-20 12:00:00'),('day-18','18','End-to-End Modernization: 3-Stage Clean Architecture Refactoring, 29-Route Playwright Mobile Audit & Zero-Defect UX Stabilization','September 24, 2026','Executed comprehensive 3-stage clean architecture modernization across 29 routes, enforced PHP 8.2 strict typing, engineered an automated headless Playwright mobile audit suite, eliminated the blank reveal-state trap, and resolved mobile overflow barriers to certify institutional production readiness.','{"id":"day-18","sprint_number":"18","sprint_badge":"DAY 18 · CLEAN ARCHITECTURE & FULL MOBILE AUDIT","title":"End-to-End Modernization: 3-Stage Clean Architecture Refactoring, 29-Route Playwright Mobile Audit & Zero-Defect UX Stabilization","date":"September 24, 2026","read_time":"9 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Executed comprehensive 3-stage clean architecture modernization across 29 routes, enforced PHP 8.2 strict typing, engineered an automated headless Playwright mobile audit suite, eliminated the blank reveal-state trap, and resolved mobile overflow barriers to certify institutional production readiness.","tags":["Clean Architecture","Stage 1-3 Refactoring","Playwright Mobile Audit","PHP 8.2 Modernization","TypeSafe Jev Gate","Mobile UX Stabilization","Zero-Defect Quality"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-18.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>September 24 marked the culmination of our full-stack codebase overhaul. We unified our 3-stage clean architecture modernization across all 29 portal routes, engineered an automated headless Playwright test harness at mobile phone viewport (390×844) across both light and dark themes, uncovered and solved the elusive ''Nothing is showing here'' blank reveal trap, and stabilized all mobile touch interactions, typography scales, and modal viewports.</p><p>Following our initial feature sprints, the codebase required architectural distillation to eliminate monolithic scripts, enforce strict type contracts, and guarantee absolute reliability on handheld student devices. With thousands of undergraduates accessing campus employment opportunities on mobile smartphones, ensuring an uncompromising, responsive, zero-defect user experience was our paramount priority.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-layers-fill text-accent me-2''></i>3-Stage Clean Architecture Modernization</h5><p>We executed a disciplined three-phase structural refactoring without disrupting runtime features: in <strong>Stage 1</strong>, monolithic page controllers were decoupled into dedicated domain services and clean presentation view partials; in <strong>Stage 2</strong>, we updated the runtime to PHP 8.2 standards, adding strict type declarations, typed return signatures, and replacing loose equality with strict identity operators (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>===</code>); in <strong>Stage 3</strong>, oversized routines were decomposed into modular, cohesive single-responsibility functions.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-phone-fill text-accent me-2''></i>29-Route Headless Playwright Mobile Audit</h5><p>Rather than relying on manual ad-hoc testing, we engineered an automated Playwright Chromium audit suite. Running against an emulated 390×844 mobile viewport with touch support and device pixel ratio of 2, the suite captured over 60 high-resolution full-page and above-the-fold screenshots across every public, student, employer, and administrative route in both Light and Dark color schemes.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-bug-fill text-accent me-2''></i>Diagnosing and Eliminating the Mobile Reveal-State Trap</h5><p>The automated audit revealed a critical UX defect: on high-volume tables such as User Management, Category Configurations, and Employer Applicants, entire rosters appeared completely blank. Forensic DOM inspection identified that <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>.reveal-fade-rise</code> initialized containers with <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>opacity: 0</code>. On mobile viewports, large table containers exceeded the IntersectionObserver scroll threshold and remained permanently invisible. We implemented a responsive CSS override guaranteeing immediate visibility (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>opacity: 1 !important</code>) on mobile viewports while tuning desktop observer margins for seamless pre-scroll reveals.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-sliders text-accent me-2''></i>Precision Mobile UI Stabilization &amp; Modal Ergonomics</h5><p>We eliminated multi-line button wrapping across registration personas and job posting steppers, engineered horizontal scrollable containment for the DevBlog navigation cluster and 17 step dots, enforced 33px clearance between long sprint badges and modal close controls, and restored interactive in-modal previous/next navigation buttons (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>#devblog-modal-prev-btn</code> / <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>#devblog-modal-next-btn</code>) for frictionless mobile reading.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-shield-check text-accent me-2''></i>TypeSafe Clean Architecture Certification (0.8800)</h5><p>Every commit across this stabilization sprint was certified through the TypeSafe System One (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>jev-gate</code>) automated quality gate, scoring <strong>0.8800</strong> (exceeding the strict 0.8500 clean architecture threshold). All 29 routes passed runtime execution tests with zero warnings, certifying full production readiness.</p>","key_takeaways":["Executed 3-stage clean architecture modernization: extracted domain services, enforced PHP 8.2 types, and decomposed monoliths.","Built automated Playwright Chromium test suite capturing 60+ mobile screenshots across all 29 routes in dual themes.","Eliminated the mobile reveal-fade-rise opacity trap, ensuring data tables and forms render immediately on all mobile screens.","Eliminated 2-liner button wrapping, pinned modal close controls with 33px clearance, and restored in-modal daily log navigation.","Certified 0.8800 clean architecture under TypeSafe System One (jev-gate) and 100% pass on 29 runtime route tests."],"tech_stack":["PHP 8.2 Strict Types","Playwright Chromium Engine","TypeSafe System One (Jev 1.13)","CSS Custom Properties & Media Queries","IntersectionObserver API","Bootstrap 5.3 Responsive Grid"]}','2026-09-23 12:00:00'),('day-19','19','Comprehensive Realism & Workflow Intelligence: 30-Account Production Datastore, Notification Flexbox Stabilization, Verification Triage Engine & High-Fidelity Registrar Profile Diff System','September 25, 2026','Scaled the portal datastore to 30 production personas across 11 colleges with verifiable resumes and schedules, stabilized the in-app notification dropdown by eliminating flexbox minimum sizing clipping, curated and integrated 10 topic-tailored requisition visuals, integrated the Verification Triage & Candidate Schedule Availability engine with institutional guardrails, and re-engineered the administrative student profile diff system with live baseline record merging and accurate proof file resolution.','{"id":"day-19","sprint_number":"19","sprint_badge":"DAY 19 · PRODUCTION REALISM, NOTIFICATIONS, REGISTRAR DIFF & VERIFICATION TRIAGE","title":"Comprehensive Realism & Workflow Intelligence: 30-Account Production Datastore, Notification Flexbox Stabilization, Verification Triage Engine & High-Fidelity Registrar Profile Diff System","date":"September 25, 2026","read_time":"11 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Scaled the portal datastore to 30 production personas across 11 colleges with verifiable resumes and schedules, stabilized the in-app notification dropdown by eliminating flexbox minimum sizing clipping, curated and integrated 10 topic-tailored requisition visuals, integrated the Verification Triage & Candidate Schedule Availability engine with institutional guardrails, and re-engineered the administrative student profile diff system with live baseline record merging and accurate proof file resolution.","tags":["Production Data Scaling","Notification Engine","CSS Flexbox Stabilization","Schedule Availability Engine","Verification Queue Triage","Schedule Availability Dossier","Registrar Profile Diff","Academic Identity Lock","Institutional Governance","Playwright E2E Testing","Zero-Defect UX"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-19.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>September 25 marked an essential evolutionary leap for the KLD Campus Job Posting System. We moved from synthetic, sparse prototyping fixtures to an authentic, high-fidelity institutional datastore featuring 30 verified personas, resolved an intricate flexbox minimum sizing clipping defect within our real-time notification dropdown, procured 10 high-resolution topic-accurate visual assets for all newly added job requisitions, incorporated the Verification Queue Triage and Candidate Schedule Availability engine with institutional guardrails, and completely re-engineered the administrative profile verification diff inspector to guarantee seamless credential comparisons.</p><p>As our system neared comprehensive operational testing, a primary operational challenge emerged: evaluating the platform under genuine campus workload conditions. Testing application pipelines, verification queues, and role-based permissions required realistic academic representations rather than placeholder accounts. Today''s sprint systematically eliminated all synthetic gaps across every tier of the application while augmenting institutional decision-makers with deterministic advisory metrics.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-people-fill text-accent me-2''></i>1. High-Fidelity Multi-Persona Datastore (30 Verified Accounts)</h5><p>We expanded our user datastore from 10 to <strong>30 distinct accounts</strong> across all university constituencies: <strong>14 student assistants</strong> enrolled in diverse degree programs (BS Information Systems, BS Computer Science, BS Nursing, BS Information Technology, BS Accountancy, BS Civil Engineering, BA Communication, BS Hospitality Management, BS Psychology, Bachelor of Elementary Education, and BS Midwifery); <strong>15 campus employers</strong> spanning 8 official university departments (Registrar, MIS, Guidance Center, Library, Science & Nursing Laboratories, Athletics Unit, Scholarship Office, Cashier & Bursar) and 7 accredited commercial partners (TechVanguard Solutions, Dasma Creative Media, Campus Cafe, Apex Robotics, GreenLeaf Bookstore, Cavite BPO Solutions, CodeCrafted Labs); and <strong>1 System Administrator</strong>.</p><p>Every student profile was enriched with comprehensive demographic records, genuine academic email formats, GPA/GWA standings, real shift availability constraints, detailed autobiographical statements, verified skill matrices, and authentic PDF resumes generated and stored directly within <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>uploads/resumes/</code>. To accelerate role switching during institutional demonstrations, we integrated a fast single-hop persona switcher directly into the login interface, backed by an interactive searchable credential directory.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-bell-fill text-accent me-2''></i>2. Notification Engine &amp; Dropdown Flexbox Stabilization</h5><p>Forensic inspection of the user navigation header revealed a subtle yet critical CSS layout bug: when notification titles exceeded a certain length (such as <em>''Interview Scheduled: Computer Lab Assistant''</em>), the title text pushed the timestamp badge (<em>''2d ago''</em>) and unread green indicator dot completely beyond the 380px boundary of the dropdown card. Because <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>.notification-dropdown-menu</code> employs <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>overflow: hidden</code>, the entire right section of the notification card was clipped off, slicing words mid-character and completely hiding vital temporal indicators.</p><p>We traced the root cause to standard CSS flexbox sizing behavior: by default, flex child items have a computed <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>min-width: auto</code>. Because utility class <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>.min-w-0</code> was absent from our component stylesheets, the inner flex containers expanded to match the natural width of long text strings rather than enforcing container boundaries. We resolved this across both server-rendered templates (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>includes-navbar-view.php</code>) and dynamic client-side pollers (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>notifications.js</code>) by introducing explicit zero minimum-width constraints, encapsulating items with <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>.notification-item-content</code> (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>min-width: 0; flex: 1 1 0%</code>), enforcing ellipsis truncation on <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>.notification-item-title</code>, fixing <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>flex-shrink: 0</code> on <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>.notification-item-time</code>, and adding native HTML <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>title</code> attributes so users can hover over any truncated heading to view the full announcement.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-image-fill text-accent me-2''></i>3. Dedicated Visual Assets for Requisitions 11–20</h5><p>To eliminate generic visual repetition across our expanded 20-job catalogue, we curated and integrated 10 topic-accurate, royalty-free photographic assets (900×600 aspect ratio) directly into <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>assets/img/jobs/</code> (job-11.jpg through job-20.jpg). Each image visually grounds its specific campus work-study requisition: algorithmic coding tutoring, clinical nursing simulation ward maintenance, psychological guidance consultations, scholarship paperwork encoding, dual-monitor React web engineering, digital creative studio illustration, bookstore cashiering, sports tournament athletics coordination, emergency clinic first aid standby, and customer care helpdesk operations. All images were mapped into database seeds and verified with zero broken image links across all catalogue views.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-shield-lock-fill text-accent me-2''></i>4. High-Fidelity Student Profile Diff &amp; Verification System</h5><p>When administrators reviewed student profile change requests in User Management, an inspection modal defect caused comparison tables to render empty dashes (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>—</code>) across all fields and falsely display <em>''No Valid Document Found''</em>. Our audit pinpointed two critical flaws: first, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>file_exists(__DIR__ . ''/../'' . $proof)</code> evaluated relative to the view template directory rather than the application root, failing to locate genuine attachments in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>uploads/proofs/</code>; second, older stored request payloads only recorded delta keys (e.g., modified course or year level), leaving other demographic fields unpopulated in strict table loops.</p><p>We re-engineered the inspection modal in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>admin-users-view.php</code> by fixing the document path resolution to <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>dirname(__DIR__, 2) . ''/'' . ltrim($proof, ''/'')</code>, ensuring instant preview generation for both PDF Certificates of Registration (COR) and high-resolution PSA birth certificate image scans. Furthermore, we implemented baseline profile inheritance: whenever a request snapshot is opened, the system dynamically merges the live student record (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>get_user_by_id</code>) with the requested changes. As a result, the student''s full academic identity is permanently visible, and only the modified fields are highlighted with eye-catching <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>MODIFIED</code> badges and bold green accents. We complemented this with 5 realistic student requests (#REQ-0001 through #REQ-0005) covering degree shifting, mid-year level progression, and official legal name corrections.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-clipboard-check text-accent me-2''></i>5. Institutional Verification Triage &amp; Schedule Availability Engine</h5><p>To alleviate administrative fatigue and streamline the onboarding of applicants, we engineered the <strong>Verification Triage &amp; Schedule Availability Engine</strong> (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>includes/services/system-checks.php</code>). Rooted in procedural academic principles, it provides transparent decision support. All statutory authority remains exclusively in the hands of university officials.</p><p>At the administrative level, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>get_verification_triage()</code> aggregates pending accounts and student profile modification requests, computing instantaneous document completeness scores (0–100%) and classifying queue items into three deterministic tiers: <strong>Ready</strong> (100% complete, verified attachments and valid IDs), <strong>Review</strong> (minor non-blocking caveats or short justification statements), and <strong>Blocked</strong> (missing critical mandatory documents, such as lack of a Certificate of Registration or business permit). In <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>admin/users.php</code>, this renders as an interactive <em>Verification Queue Triage</em> panel with dynamic score badges, diagnostic dot-flags, and one-click direct inspection deep-links.</p><p>For campus employers evaluating applicants, the system parses the student''s 18-slot weekly schedule availability matrix (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>get_schedule_summary()</code>), evaluating total workload capacity against the university''s statutory 20-hour academic cap. Candidates are categorized into <strong>Optimal Fit (20h+)</strong>, <strong>Moderate Fit (12–16h)</strong>, <strong>Limited Fit (4–8h)</strong>, and <strong>High Schedule Risk (0h / Conflict)</strong>. On the employer roster (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>employer/applicants.php</code>), supervisors can filter and sort candidates directly by schedule availability fit. Meanwhile, on <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>student/job-details.php</code>, students receive instant read-only schedule alignment insights before submitting their applications.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-check-circle-fill text-accent me-2''></i>6. Rigorous End-to-End Test Automation &amp; Certification</h5><p>We bracketed all modifications with automated Playwright browser tests and CLI diagnostics: clean database migration (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>php database/migrate.php --clean</code>) executed with 100% success across 9 tables; all 29 portal routes passed automated runtime checks with zero warnings or errors; and our automated Playwright suites (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>profile-diff.spec.ts</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>notif-dropdown.spec.ts</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>roster-filter.spec.ts</code>, and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>smoke.spec.ts</code>) verified that the notification dropdown, image loaders, schedule filters, candidate dossiers, and diff comparison modals render flawlessly without horizontal clipping or missing data.</p>","key_takeaways":["Expanded datastore to 30 institutional accounts (14 students across 11 colleges, 15 campus employers, 1 administrator) with realistic bios, skills, and genuine PDF resumes.","Scaled active requisitions from 10 to 20 across 6 job categories and curated 10 topic-accurate 900×600 photographic assets in assets/img/jobs/.","Forensically diagnosed and eliminated the notification dropdown clipping bug by introducing .min-w-0 and modular flex constraints (.notification-item-content, .notification-item-title, .notification-item-time).","Re-engineered the administrative profile update diff modal: fixed relative path resolution for proof attachments and integrated baseline merging with live student records so comparisons never display empty dashes.","Rebuilt profile_requests fixtures with 5 realistic student cases (#REQ-0001 to #REQ-0005) featuring authentic COR and PSA proofs, change justifications, and audit trails.","Architected Institutional Verification Queue Triage (Ready, Review, Blocked) and Candidate Schedule Availability engine.","Integrated Schedule Availability fit columns, dynamic filtering, and availability sorting into the employer roster, verified via Playwright E2E suites.","Certified zero regressions across 29 runtime routes and 100% pass rate on automated Playwright E2E test suites."],"tech_stack":["PHP 8.2 & PDO MySQL (3NF Schema)","Schedule Availability Engine","Verification Queue Triage Matrix","CSS Flexbox & CSS Custom Properties","Bootstrap 5.3 Modals & Dropdowns","Playwright Chromium Headless Engine","JSON Relational Seed Migration Engine","Unsplash Curated Media Assets"]}','2026-09-24 12:00:00'),('day-20','20','Institutional Compliance & Visual Intelligence: Full RA 10173 Overhaul, NVIDIA NIM Free-Tier AI Model Training Transparency, Chart.js Visualizations & 16-Section Work Guidelines v2.4','September 26, 2026','Executed comprehensive institutional compliance and visual architecture expansion: overhauled the Terms of Service into a 16-section regulatory blueprint with academic priority protections and DTR fraud safeguards, enriched the Data Privacy Policy under RA 10173 with mandatory NVIDIA NIM free-tier AI model training transparency disclosures, integrated Chart.js 4.4+ interactive data visualizations into the core technology stack and knowledge graph with dynamic cache-busting, and introduced persistent AI privacy warnings across the 3D robot companion and fullscreen studio.','{"id":"day-20","sprint_number":"20","sprint_badge":"DAY 20 · STATUTORY PRIVACY, NVIDIA AI TRANSPARENCY, CHART.JS & TERMS v2.4","title":"Institutional Compliance & Visual Intelligence: Full RA 10173 Overhaul, NVIDIA NIM Free-Tier AI Model Training Transparency, Chart.js Visualizations & 16-Section Work Guidelines v2.4","date":"September 26, 2026","read_time":"10 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Executed comprehensive institutional compliance and visual architecture expansion: overhauled the Terms of Service into a 16-section regulatory blueprint with academic priority protections and DTR fraud safeguards, enriched the Data Privacy Policy under RA 10173 with mandatory NVIDIA NIM free-tier AI model training transparency disclosures, integrated Chart.js 4.4+ interactive data visualizations into the core technology stack and knowledge graph with dynamic cache-busting, and introduced persistent AI privacy warnings across the 3D robot companion and fullscreen studio.","tags":["Terms of Service v2.4","Data Privacy Act (RA 10173)","NVIDIA NIM AI Cloud Transparency","AI Model Training Disclosures","Chart.js 4.4 Data Visualizations","Technical Architecture Knowledge Graph","20-Hour Weekly Work Limit","Academic Moratorium & Exam Leave","Workplace Confidentiality & NDAs","Cache-Busting Asset Versioning"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-20.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>September 26 represents a foundational institutional milestone for the KLD Campus Job Posting System. Shifting our focus to statutory accountability, regulatory governance, and architectural clarity, we executed a full-spectrum upgrade across our legal policies and technology showcase: transforming our brief Terms of Service into a 16-section university-grade framework, expanding our Data Privacy Policy under RA 10173 to provide absolute transparency regarding NVIDIA NIM free-tier AI model training, integrating Chart.js 4.4+ interactive visualizations into our core tech stack and knowledge graph, and engineering real-time cache-busting asset versioning to guarantee instant client updates.</p><p>As university systems scale from classroom prototypes to official campus infrastructure, technical prowess must be matched by legal rigor and ethical transparency. With active student assistants handling administrative files, department heads creating requisitions, and AI assistants fielding inquiries, today''s sprint established an unshakeable institutional foundation that protects student welfare, academic priorities, and data sovereignty.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-file-earmark-check-fill text-accent me-2''></i>1. University Terms of Service &amp; Campus Work Guidelines (Policy v2.4)</h5><p>Our previously concise terms page was completely re-architected into a rigorous <strong>16-section institutional policy document</strong> formally aligned with the KLD Student Handbook, CHED student assistantship circulars, and the City Government of Dasmariñas. Key enhancements include: explicit undergraduate academic eligibility (minimum 12 units enrolled, 2.50 GWA, and good moral standing); an immutable <strong>20-hour weekly labor cap</strong> during class terms with an exception window up to 40 hours during official semester breaks upon SASO endorsement; a single-account institutional identity rule; mandatory 14-day candidate review windows for department employers; strict Daily Time Record (DTR) attendance verification with an uncompromising zero-tolerance fraud clause; an examination moratorium guaranteeing shift suspensions during midterm and final exam weeks without penalty; comprehensive student assistant non-disclosure covenants protecting campus records under RA 10173 and RA 10175; and full institutional alignment with the Safe Spaces Act (RA 11313) backed by the KLD Committee on Decorum and Investigation (CODI).</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-cpu-fill text-accent me-2''></i>2. NVIDIA NIM Free-Tier AI Model Training Transparency &amp; Data Privacy</h5><p>In accordance with statutory guidelines from the National Privacy Commission (NPC) regarding automated systems and AI sub-processors, we executed an in-depth expansion of our <strong>Data Privacy Policy (RA 10173)</strong>. We introduced an explicit, prominent disclosure detailing our integration with <strong>NVIDIA Corporation''s NVIDIA NIM Cloud API</strong> (<code>https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1</code>). Users are transparently notified that under developer/free-tier evaluation API terms, conversational interactions and prompts may be logged, retained, and used by NVIDIA and foundation model partners (such as Meta, Mistral AI, DeepSeek, and Google) for model safety evaluation and AI training.</p><p>Crucially, we established clear data boundaries and user safeguards: users are strictly warned against inputting sensitive personal data, passwords, grades, or department records into the chat interface; we verified that official student resumes, Certificates of Registration (COR), and application dossiers reside exclusively on protected local university servers and are <em>never</em> dispatched to external AI models; we documented our zero-cloud local heuristic fallback mode; and we embedded persistent, non-intrusive AI privacy badges below both the hero robot speech bubble and the fullscreen companion studio.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-bar-chart-line-fill text-accent me-2''></i>3. Chart.js 4.4 Data Visualizations &amp; Tech Stack Integration</h5><p>To reflect the platform''s administrative analytics capabilities, we formalized the addition of <strong>Chart.js 4.4+</strong> to the project''s core technology stack across <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>package.json</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>README.md</code>, and the interactive technical knowledge graph. In administrative reports (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>admin/reports.php</code>), Chart.js powers responsive canvas-rendered hiring quota gauges, departmental vacancy distribution charts, and applicant demographic breakdowns. In <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>README.md</code>, we updated the Frontend and Architecture specifications to highlight Chart.js alongside Three.js WebGL and vanilla ES6+ script modules.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-diagram-3-fill text-accent me-2''></i>4. Interactive Knowledge Graph Enhancement &amp; Dynamic 5-Leaf Physics</h5><p>On <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>about-us.php</code>, we expanded our Obsidian-style force-directed network graph (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>assets/js/tech-graph.js</code>) from 14 to <strong>15 interconnected technologies</strong> by introducing a dedicated <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>chartjs</code> leaf node within the Frontend &amp; 3D cluster. To maintain comfortable, balanced visual hierarchy without label crowding, we re-calibrated the physics simulation: dynamically broadening the radial distribution arc to 0.82π and expanding leaf orbital distance to 70px for 5-node clusters. Clicking or hovering over the node instantly pins its analytical attributes and vector bar-chart iconography into the inspector HUD.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-arrow-repeat text-accent me-2''></i>5. Real-Time Cache-Busting Asset Versioning</h5><p>During live verification, we diagnosed a subtle client-side artifact: browsers that had previously loaded the developers page retained cached script bundles due to a static query parameter (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>?v=1.0</code>). We eliminated this latency by implementing dynamic timestamped versioning (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>?v=&lt;?= time() ?&gt;</code>) in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>about-us-view.php</code>. All connected clients now immediately receive the freshest asset bundles upon page reload, certified by our automated headless Chromium verification runs.</p>","key_takeaways":["Overhauled Terms of Service (Policy v2.4) into 16 legally sound sections incorporating 20h labor caps, DTR fraud penalties, academic exam leave, and Safe Spaces Act (RA 11313) protections.","Expanded Data Privacy Policy (RA 10173) with explicit disclosures regarding NVIDIA NIM free-tier cloud endpoints and AI model training data usage.","Established strict local data boundaries: student resumes, COR proofs, and application dossiers remain exclusively on local servers and are never transmitted to external AI models.","Added persistent AI privacy notice badges to both the hero 3D robot speech bubble and the Fullscreen AI Studio modal linking directly to statutory disclosures.","Formally added Chart.js 4.4+ to package.json, README.md technology stack, and administrative analytics reports.","Integrated Chart.js leaf node into the interactive Obsidian-style Technical Architecture Knowledge Graph with dynamic 5-leaf radial arc physics (0.82π).","Implemented dynamic timestamped cache-busting (?v=<?= time() ?>) in about-us-view.php ensuring immediate asset updates without manual cache clearing.","Verified complete end-to-end regression pass with 100% test success across all 6 Playwright smoke and health suites."],"tech_stack":["Chart.js 4.4 Data Visualization Engine","NVIDIA NIM AI Cloud Inference Gateway","Statutory Compliance (RA 10173 & RA 11313)","Obsidian Force-Directed Knowledge Graph","PHP 8.2 Modular Clean Architecture","Cache-Busting Dynamic Versioning","Vanilla ES6+ Canvas 2D & Three.js WebGL"]}','2026-09-25 12:00:00'),('day-21','21','Legal Modernization & Interactive Knowledge Graph: Numbered Legal Codex, Full-Screen Architecture Unification, Scaled Component Physics & Vector Iconography','September 27, 2026','Executed deep legal modernization and major technical architecture evolution: converted the Data Privacy Policy and Terms of Service into exhaustive university-grade legal codices with numbered clauses, eliminated colon-based key-value fragments and all em dashes in favor of natural phrasing, scaled prose typography to 1.0625rem with justified text alignment, stripped out intrusive warning badges, resolved vertical alignment issues for the NVIDIA Cloud AI privacy notice within the Fullscreen AI Studio, and unified the About Us Project Mission and Technical Architecture into an expansive full-screen force-directed knowledge graph featuring real-world architectural component weighting, in-circle vector icons, streaming data flow pulses, click shockwaves, and contextual neighbor illumination.','{"id":"day-21","sprint_number":"21","sprint_badge":"DAY 21 · LEGAL CODEX PROSE, FULL-SCREEN KNOWLEDGE GRAPH & ARCHITECTURAL SIZING","title":"Legal Modernization & Interactive Knowledge Graph: Numbered Legal Codex, Full-Screen Architecture Unification, Scaled Component Physics & Vector Iconography","date":"September 27, 2026","read_time":"12 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Executed deep legal modernization and major technical architecture evolution: converted the Data Privacy Policy and Terms of Service into exhaustive university-grade legal codices with numbered clauses, eliminated colon-based key-value fragments and all em dashes in favor of natural phrasing, scaled prose typography to 1.0625rem with justified text alignment, stripped out intrusive warning badges, resolved vertical alignment issues for the NVIDIA Cloud AI privacy notice within the Fullscreen AI Studio, and unified the About Us Project Mission and Technical Architecture into an expansive full-screen force-directed knowledge graph featuring real-world architectural component weighting, in-circle vector icons, streaming data flow pulses, click shockwaves, and contextual neighbor illumination.","tags":["Legal Policy Modernization","Data Privacy Act (RA 10173)","Terms of Service Architecture","Typography & Justified Layout","Em Dash Elimination","Fullscreen AI Studio","UI Micro-Alignment","Interactive Knowledge Graph","Technical Architecture","Full-Screen Layout Unification","Architectural Sizing & Physics","Canvas 2D Data Pulses"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-21.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>Following our statutory compliance overhaul, Day 21 delivered a dual breakthrough in legal craftsmanship and systems visualization. We transformed both the Data Privacy Policy and Terms of Service into exhaustive, formal institutional agreements with numbered clauses, banished all colon-formatted fragments and em dashes in favor of smooth grammatical prose, scaled our body typography for crystal-clear readability, enforced full text justification, resolved fine-grained UI micro-alignment issues across our Fullscreen AI Studio modal, and culminated the sprint by re-architecting the About Us page into an expansive, full-screen interactive technical architecture knowledge graph with architectural component sizing, native in-circle vector icons, streaming data flow pulses, and ripple physics.</p><p>A university platform must inspire immediate institutional trust while making its underlying engineering accessible and engaging. When students and faculty review privacy commitments or explore the system ecosystem, the interface should feel authoritative, harmonious, and technically extraordinary. Today''s sprint bridged publication-grade legal design with modern interactive systems visualization.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-file-earmark-text-fill text-accent me-2''></i>1. Transformation into Numbered Legal Codex Prose</h5><p>We systematically reworked every section of both <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>privacy.php</code> and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>terms.php</code> away from simplistic colon forms (such as bolded prefixes followed by isolated sentences) into continuous, multi-sentence legal paragraphs organized under formal numbered clauses (&sect;1.1 through &sect;16.2). Each clause now articulates institutional context, statutory references, operational responsibilities, and procedural enforcement mechanisms, elevating the platform''s compliance documentation to university-grade standards.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-fonts text-accent me-2''></i>2. Typographic Scaling &amp; Justified Text Alignment</h5><p>To eliminate eye strain and deliver a publication-quality reading experience, we upgraded our <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>.prose</code> typography in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>custom.css</code> from 15px to <strong>1.0625rem (~17px)</strong> with an expansive <strong>1.85 line-height</strong>, while increasing lead paragraphs to 1.15rem. We stripped out reducing small-text classes on body paragraphs and implemented clean, uniform text justification (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-word; hyphens: auto;</code>) across all legal paragraphs and callout cards. This provides the crisp, balanced margins characteristic of formal administrative charters.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-slash-circle text-accent me-2''></i>3. Strict Em Dash Elimination &amp; Natural Punctuation</h5><p>In accordance with clean editorial guidelines, we conducted an exhaustive sweep across the codebase to banish all em dashes (&mdash;), en dashes (&ndash;), and dash entity representations. Every parenthetical dash was replaced with natural comma phrasing, parenthetical notes, or clear grammatical connectors (such as ''to'' or ''or''), ensuring a fluid, polished cadence across all legal definitions and assistantship guidelines.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-check-circle-fill text-accent me-2''></i>4. Section 4 Header Polish &amp; Badge Cleanup</h5><p>Inside the Data Privacy Policy, we removed the intrusive yellow warning badge in Section 4 and resolved a persistent vertical misalignment between the green CPU icon and the section title. By eliminating an inherited 2.25rem top margin on headings inside <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>.card-paper</code> containers and normalizing line-height metrics, the icon and section title now sit in flawless vertical alignment.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-chat-square-quote-fill text-accent me-2''></i>5. Fullscreen AI Studio Privacy Notice Micro-Alignment</h5><p>Under the chat input bar of the Fullscreen AI Studio modal, the NVIDIA Cloud AI privacy notice previously suffered from layout distortion caused by a rigid flex row container: when the disclaimer wrapped across two lines, the shield icon hung vertically between lines and the Privacy Notice link was pushed to the far right edge. We re-engineered this notice into a unified, centered inline paragraph across both <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>index-view.php</code> and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>faqs-view.php</code>. The shield icon now aligns naturally with the text baseline, and the Privacy Notice link stays seamlessly connected to the sentence regardless of screen width.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-diagram-3-fill text-accent me-2''></i>6. Technical Architecture Knowledge Graph Evolution &amp; Full-Screen Unification</h5><p>To culminate Day 21, we unified ''Our Project Mission'' and the ''Technical Architecture'' knowledge graph on the About Us page into an expansive, full-span interactive experience utilizing the entire viewport width. Rather than uniform circles, we re-architected the canvas engine so node radii directly reflect their true architectural footprint in the system: the KLD Platform Hub anchors the center at 46px (100% scale), major domain pillars command 32px, and core heavyweight engines (PHP 8.2 MVC at 96%, MySQL InnoDB at 94%, Three.js WebGL at 86%, and NVIDIA NIM at 88%) scale proportionally above modular utilities.</p><p>We embedded native Bootstrap Icon vector glyphs directly within every circular node, implemented streaming animated data packet pulses traveling along active connection pipelines, engineered expanding click shockwaves with tactile ripple feedback, added rotating kinetic orbit rings to the platform hub and domain pillars, and introduced contextual neighbor illumination that highlights direct dependency pipelines while softly dimming unrelated nodes. The bottom inspector HUD was upgraded with a dynamic architectural tier and scale rating badge that reflects each component''s criticality in real time.</p>","key_takeaways":["Transformed Data Privacy Policy and Terms of Service from fragmented colon forms into exhaustive, numbered legal codex prose.","Eliminated all em dashes, en dashes, and dash entities across legal policies, substituting natural commas and conjunctions.","Upgraded .prose typography across custom.css to 1.0625rem with 1.85 line-height and uniform justified text alignment.","Removed the intrusive yellow warning badge in Section 4 of privacy.php and aligned the CPU icon with the section title.","Re-architected the NVIDIA Cloud AI disclosure under the Fullscreen AI Studio chat input from a fractured flex row into an inline centered paragraph.","Synchronized the aligned AI notice across index-view.php and faqs-view.php for consistent modal UI presentation.","Unified the Project Mission and Technical Architecture into an expansive full-screen showcase with responsive canvas sizing.","Engineered real-world architectural weighting for all graph nodes with in-circle vector icons, streaming data pulses, and click shockwaves.","Added contextual neighbor illumination, rotating orbit rings, and an architecture tier scale rating badge to the inspector HUD."],"tech_stack":["PHP 8.2 Clean Architecture","Canvas 2D Knowledge Graph","Force-Directed Physics","Vector Glyph Rendering","Responsive Typography System","CSS Hyphenation & Text Justification","Bootstrap Icons Micro-Alignment","Statutory Compliance (RA 10173)","Fullscreen AI Studio Chatbot"]}','2026-09-26 12:00:00'),('day-22','22','Deep Module Architecture: Introducing SessionGuard, In-Process Auth Interception, Return-To Sanitization & Verification Quarantine','September 28, 2026','Executed an architectural survey and deep-module refactor: transformed the shallow 38-line auth-check file into SessionGuard, collapsed the fragmented session state machine, eliminated unmockable process exits in favor of an interceptable redirect responder seam, hardened return-to deep linking against open redirects, encapsulated unverified email quarantine and OTP code generation, initialized our formal CONTEXT.md domain glossary, and delivered an exhaustive 20-assertion in-process test suite passing with 100% compliance.','{"id":"day-22","sprint_number":"22","sprint_badge":"DAY 22 · SESSIONGUARD ARCHITECTURE, AUTH STATE MACHINE & DOMAIN SEAMS","title":"Deep Module Architecture: Introducing SessionGuard, In-Process Auth Interception, Return-To Sanitization & Verification Quarantine","date":"September 28, 2026","read_time":"10 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Executed an architectural survey and deep-module refactor: transformed the shallow 38-line auth-check file into SessionGuard, collapsed the fragmented session state machine, eliminated unmockable process exits in favor of an interceptable redirect responder seam, hardened return-to deep linking against open redirects, encapsulated unverified email quarantine and OTP code generation, initialized our formal CONTEXT.md domain glossary, and delivered an exhaustive 20-assertion in-process test suite passing with 100% compliance.","tags":["SessionGuard Architecture","Deep Modules & Codebase Design","Authentication State Machine","Verification Quarantine","Return-To Deep Linking","Open Redirect Protection","In-Process Testing Seam","Domain Modeling (CONTEXT.md)"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-22.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>Following our legal modernization and knowledge graph expansion, Day 22 initiated a focused architectural evolution across the platform''s authentication perimeter. Guided by deep-module design principles, we replaced the shallow, pass-through auth-check helper with a unified SessionGuard engine, collapsed the fragmented authentication and OTP verification state machines, eliminated unmockable process exit side effects with an interceptable responder seam, hardened return-to deep linking against open redirect exploits, initialized the platform''s formal domain model in CONTEXT.md, and validated the overhaul with a comprehensive 20-assertion in-process test suite.</p><p>In high-leverage application engineering, modules should be deep: presenting a concise, intuitive interface that conceals substantial internal complexity. Prior to this sprint, 36 controllers across the codebase relied on a superficial helper file that merely computed dashboard URLs, while critical authentication checks and OTP handoffs were duplicated across login, registration, and role controllers. Today''s sprint concentrated this scattered complexity behind a single robust authority.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-shield-lock-fill text-accent me-2''></i>1. Transforming auth-check.php into the SessionGuard Engine</h5><p>We deepened <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>includes/auth-check.php</code> from a 38-line redirect stub into <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>SessionGuard</code>. This module serves as the single source of truth for request authentication, role-based access control (RBAC), and user session lifecycle management. Rather than forcing callers to manage session arrays and manually resolve nested directory paths, callers across all tiers now invoke <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>SessionGuard::protect()</code> with full backward compatibility preserved for legacy helper shims.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-arrow-repeat text-accent me-2''></i>2. Eliminating Unmockable Process Exits via Interceptable Seam</h5><p>A longstanding impediment to test automation was that legacy authentication functions called <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>header(''Location: ...''); exit;</code> directly, instantly halting PHP CLI test runners and headless evaluation harnesses. We engineered an interceptable HTTP responder seam via <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>SessionGuard::setRedirectHandler()</code>. In web production, requests execute standard HTTP headers; in testing environments, redirection attempts, HTTP status codes, and flash messages are cleanly captured in memory without terminating the test runner.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-link-45deg text-accent me-2''></i>3. Hardened Return-To Deep Linking &amp; Open-Redirect Protection</h5><p>When unauthenticated students attempt to access restricted application workflows (such as applying for a specific job vacancy), the platform must preserve their target destination across the login flow. We implemented automated, sanitized return-to resolution that extracts the relative request URI and appends a safe <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>?next=</code> parameter. To prevent open redirect vulnerabilities, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>SessionGuard::sanitizeReturnTo()</code> rigorously validates destination paths, stripping protocol schemes (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>https:</code>), protocol-relative slashes (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>//</code>), and script execution vectors.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-envelope-check-fill text-accent me-2''></i>4. Encapsulation of Verification Quarantine &amp; OTP Lifecycle</h5><p>Previously, when unverified users signed in or registered, the setup of pending verification sessions, six-digit OTP generation, and email dispatch was duplicated across <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>login.php</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>register.php</code>, and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>user-service.php</code>. We encapsulated this entire state machine within <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>SessionGuard::quarantineForVerification()</code> and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>SessionGuard::graduateVerification()</code>, ensuring that unverified accounts are securely quarantined and smoothly elevated upon code submission.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-journal-text text-accent me-2''></i>5. Formal Domain Glossary (CONTEXT.md) &amp; Comprehensive Test Harness</h5><p>To establish long-term architectural clarity, we inaugurated the project''s official domain model in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>CONTEXT.md</code>, recording canonical definitions for SessionGuard, Verification Quarantine, Return-To Target, and Role Dashboard. We accompanied the implementation with an automated unit test harness (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>tests/test-session-guard.php</code>) containing 20 granular assertions that verify open-redirect immunity, in-process redirect interception, role permission gating, and session graduation with 100% pass rate.</p>","key_takeaways":["Deepened includes/auth-check.php into SessionGuard, consolidating auth gating, RBAC, and session state.","Eliminated unmockable exit statements using an interceptable redirect responder seam for CLI and unit testing.","Engineered automated return-to deep linking with strict open-redirect sanitization against external schemes.","Encapsulated unverified account quarantine, six-digit OTP creation, and session graduation into a single state machine.","Inaugurated CONTEXT.md defining formal domain language for authentication and session lifecycle concepts.","Created a 20-assertion in-process unit test harness passing with 100% success alongside the JEV structural gate."],"tech_stack":["PHP 8.2 Deep Module Architecture","SessionGuard State Machine","Cryptographic OTP Dispatch","In-Process HTTP Responder Seam","Open-Redirect Sanitization Engine","Domain Modeling & CONTEXT.md"]}','2026-09-27 12:00:00'),('day-23','23','Deep Architecture Trilogy: ApplicationService Invariants, AttachmentStore Swappable Seam & DatastoreManager Fixture Orchestration','September 29, 2026','Completed the deep-module architectural transformation across the entire platform core: extracted ApplicationService with the RequisitionEligibility domain value object, eliminated row-hydrating applicant count queries, unified five scattered upload routines into AttachmentStore with a swappable StorageAdapter seam and binary magic byte sniffing, encapsulated fixture resets and eradicated runtime DDL overhead with DatastoreManager, updated our canonical CONTEXT.md domain model, and validated all four architectural pillars with 72 automated assertions across four dedicated test suites passing with 100% compliance.','{"id":"day-23","sprint_number":"23","sprint_badge":"DAY 23 · APPLICATION INVARIANTS, STORAGE ADAPTER SEAM & DATASTORE LIFECYCLE","title":"Deep Architecture Trilogy: ApplicationService Invariants, AttachmentStore Swappable Seam & DatastoreManager Fixture Orchestration","date":"September 29, 2026","read_time":"12 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Completed the deep-module architectural transformation across the entire platform core: extracted ApplicationService with the RequisitionEligibility domain value object, eliminated row-hydrating applicant count queries, unified five scattered upload routines into AttachmentStore with a swappable StorageAdapter seam and binary magic byte sniffing, encapsulated fixture resets and eradicated runtime DDL overhead with DatastoreManager, updated our canonical CONTEXT.md domain model, and validated all four architectural pillars with 72 automated assertions across four dedicated test suites passing with 100% compliance.","tags":["ApplicationService Architecture","RequisitionEligibility Value Object","AttachmentStore & StorageAdapter Seam","Binary Magic Byte Inspection","DatastoreManager & Fixture Lifecycle","Runtime DDL Elimination","Domain Modeling (CONTEXT.md)","Deep Modules & Codebase Design"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-23.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>Following Day 22''s foundation with SessionGuard, Day 23 completed the deep-module architectural transformation across the remaining core subsystems of the platform. We extracted a dedicated ApplicationService featuring the RequisitionEligibility value object to govern vacancy application invariants, eliminated full-row hydrating applicant count queries in favor of atomic SQL aggregates, unified five fragmented file upload helpers into AttachmentStore backed by a swappable StorageAdapter seam and pure-PHP magic byte inspection, and eradicated runtime DDL overhead while centralizing fixture lifecycles with DatastoreManager. Together, these enhancements deliver unparalleled codebase locality, testability, and architectural leverage.</p><p>A well-architected system achieves deep modules by providing concise, high-leverage interfaces that hide intricate implementation mechanisms. Prior to this sprint, application eligibility logic was duplicated across controllers and views, file uploads were handled by copy-pasted procedural functions with hardcoded upload paths, and testing environments faced severe impedance from runtime schema queries and inline file mutations. Today''s sprint resolved each of these architectural debts in sequence.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-file-earmark-person-fill text-accent me-2''></i>1. Candidate 2: ApplicationService &amp; the RequisitionEligibility Value Object</h5><p>We relieved <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>job-service.php</code> of its ballooning responsibilities by creating <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>ApplicationService</code>. Central to this module is the <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>RequisitionEligibility</code> value object, which encapsulates the complete business rule matrix for determining whether an authenticated student may apply for a vacancy. Status states (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>active</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>closed</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>draft</code>), application deadlines, vacancy capacity (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>slots_total</code> vs <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>slots_filled</code>), institutional student verification, and prior submission status are now evaluated through a single call to <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>ApplicationService::checkEligibility()</code>.</p><p>Furthermore, we eliminated the performance bottleneck where callers invoked <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>count(get_applications())</code> to display applicant counts. In high-traffic campus job boards, fetching and hydrating thousands of candidate records simply to calculate a count wastes memory and database bandwidth. We replaced this with <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>ApplicationService::getApplicantCount()</code>, running atomic <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>SELECT COUNT(*)</code> queries with strict index utilization.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-folder-symlink-fill text-accent me-2''></i>2. Candidate 3: AttachmentStore &amp; the Swappable StorageAdapter Seam</h5><p>Next, we targeted the fragmented document and image storage pipelines. Previously, five distinct functions (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>save_uploaded_permit</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>save_uploaded_proof</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>save_uploaded_resume</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>save_uploaded_job_photo</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>save_uploaded_category_photo</code>) duplicated 124 lines of extension verification, directory creation, and random prefixing. We consolidated these into <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>AttachmentStore</code>, organizing uploads by formal Storage Collections with validated MIME and extension policies.</p><p>To solve the fundamental testing friction where PHP''s native <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>move_uploaded_file()</code> only succeeds under HTTP POST requests, we engineered the <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>StorageAdapter</code> seam. In production, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>HttpStorageAdapter</code> performs secure multipart upload moves; in headless test environments, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>LocalDiskAdapter</code> allows test harnesses to upload and persist mock binary fixtures without needing an HTTP web server. Additionally, we embedded pure-PHP magic byte inspection in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>AttachmentStore::detectMimeType()</code>, validating PNG, JPEG, GIF, PDF, WEBP, and Office XML headers directly even when native C-extensions like <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>fileinfo</code> are unavailable.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-database-gear text-accent me-2''></i>3. Candidate 4: DatastoreManager &amp; Eradicating Runtime DDL Overhead</h5><p>An architectural audit revealed two critical leaks in datastore lifecycle management: First, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>login.php</code> contained 43 lines of inline demo fixture resetting, session destruction, and file copying. Second, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>user-service.php</code> was executing DDL queries (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>SHOW COLUMNS FROM users</code> and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS</code>) during hot runtime user flows (every user registration, password reset, and OTP email dispatch).</p><p>We introduced <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>DatastoreManager</code> to encapsulate fixture synchronization, system mode switching (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>demo</code> vs <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>real</code>), and session state reconciliation behind a unified authority. Inline reset code in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>login.php</code> collapsed from 43 lines down to a clean, declarative call to <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>DatastoreManager::resetToDemo()</code>. Furthermore, runtime DDL was extracted into <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>DatastoreManager::ensureSchema()</code> with in-process memoization, eliminating all redundant schema inspection queries from hot runtime query paths while ensuring complete compatibility.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-journal-bookmark-fill text-accent me-2''></i>4. Formal Domain Model (CONTEXT.md) &amp; 72-Assertion Test Rig</h5><p>As these architectural concepts solidified, we documented their canonical definitions in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>CONTEXT.md</code>, adding formalized entries for <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>ApplicationService</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>RequisitionEligibility</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>Vacancy Capacity</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>AttachmentStore</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>Storage Collection</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>StorageResult</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>DatastoreManager</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>Dataset Mode</code>, and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>Baseline Fixture</code>.</p><p>We validated the entire architectural overhaul with four dedicated in-process test suites: <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>tests/test-session-guard.php</code> (20/20), <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>tests/test-application-service.php</code> (21/21), <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>tests/test-attachment-store.php</code> (16/16), and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>tests/test-datastore-manager.php</code> (15/15). Across all 72 granular assertions, the platform achieved 100% pass rates, zero runtime warnings, and unanimous clearance under the JEV strict structural gate.</p>","key_takeaways":["Extracted ApplicationService and RequisitionEligibility value object, reducing job-service.php and centralizing candidate eligibility rules.","Replaced full-row hydration in applicant count checks with atomic SQL SELECT COUNT(*) aggregates.","Unified five fragmented file upload routines into AttachmentStore backed by a swappable StorageAdapter seam and binary magic byte sniffing.","Architected DatastoreManager to encapsulate dataset mode toggling and eliminate repetitive runtime DDL queries across OTP paths.","Expanded CONTEXT.md with rigorous domain terminology for RequisitionEligibility, AttachmentStore, and DatastoreManager.","Delivered 72 automated assertions across 4 unit test suites passing with 100% compliance alongside the strict JEV architectural gate."],"tech_stack":["PHP 8.2 Deep Architecture","RequisitionEligibility Domain Value Object","StorageAdapter Interface & Seam","Binary Magic Byte Detection","DatastoreManager Fixture Orchestration","Runtime DDL Elimination","CONTEXT.md Domain Modeling"]}','2026-09-28 12:00:00'),('day-24','24','Culmination & Defense Readiness: Non-Destructive Soft-Delete Archival, Student Candidate Autonomy, Verification Hardening & Complete Defense Knowledge Vault','September 30, 2026','Approaching the final capstone defense milestone, Day 24 delivers the definitive stability and audit-integrity upgrade across the entire platform: replaced all hard destructive deletions with a non-destructive soft-delete archival architecture across jobs, categories, bulletins, and user accounts; granted student candidate autonomy via application withdrawal and seamless re-submission; established frictionless in-session OTP verification passcodes for offline testing environments; implemented API key masking and Apache directory shielding; and finalized the comprehensive Obsidian-compatible defense walkthrough vault covering all 50+ controllers, templates, and services.','{"id":"day-24","sprint_number":"24","sprint_badge":"DAY 24 · NON-DESTRUCTIVE ARCHIVAL, CANDIDATE AUTONOMY, SECURITY SHIELDING & FINAL DEFENSE READINESS","title":"Culmination & Defense Readiness: Non-Destructive Soft-Delete Archival, Student Candidate Autonomy, Verification Hardening & Complete Defense Knowledge Vault","date":"September 30, 2026","read_time":"12 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Approaching the final capstone defense milestone, Day 24 delivers the definitive stability and audit-integrity upgrade across the entire platform: replaced all hard destructive deletions with a non-destructive soft-delete archival architecture across jobs, categories, bulletins, and user accounts; granted student candidate autonomy via application withdrawal and seamless re-submission; established frictionless in-session OTP verification passcodes for offline testing environments; implemented API key masking and Apache directory shielding; and finalized the comprehensive Obsidian-compatible defense walkthrough vault covering all 50+ controllers, templates, and services.","tags":["Non-Destructive Archival Architecture","Soft-Delete & Audit Trail Preservation","Candidate Application Withdrawal","Account Suspension & Deactivation","Administrative Restoration Authority","Verification Passcode Fallback","API Key Masking & Shielding","Obsidian Defense Knowledge Vault"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-24.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>As our team nears the final capstone defense milestone for the KLD Campus Job Posting System, Day 24 establishes the definitive stability, audit-integrity, and security perimeter across the entire platform. In response to our professor''s institutional compliance mandate, we replaced all hard destructive deletions with an enterprise non-destructive soft-delete archival architecture across jobs, categories, dispatches, and user accounts. Furthermore, we granted student applicants full candidate autonomy via application withdrawal and seamless re-submission, engineered a frictionless in-session OTP verification fallback for offline defense evaluation, fortified application secrets with API key masking and Apache directory shielding, and finalized a comprehensive 50-file Obsidian defense review vault.</p><p>In institutional enterprise systems, physical deletion of records is an architectural anti-pattern that destroys legal compliance, breaks relational foreign-key integrity, and erases audit trails. When an employer closes a vacancy or a department updates an announcement, candidate applications, interview appointments, and compliance logs must remain preserved for university accreditation. Today''s sprint formalized this philosophy into every layer of our database and service architecture.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-archive-fill text-accent me-2''></i>1. The Institutional ''Archive Only'' Mandate: Non-Destructive Archival Architecture</h5><p>We expanded <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>database/schema.sql</code> and updated our domain services (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>job-service.php</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>system-service.php</code>) with indexed <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>is_archived</code> (BOOLEAN) and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>archived_at</code> (DATETIME) columns across <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>categories</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>jobs</code>, and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>updates</code>. Destructive <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>DELETE</code> queries were deprecated and redirected to safe archival updates. In the administrative and employer dashboards, we introduced dedicated dual-tab navigation allowing users to toggle seamlessly between <strong>Active</strong> listings and <strong>Archived</strong> repositories.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-person-x-fill text-accent me-2''></i>2. Student Candidate Autonomy &amp; Withdrawn Invariants</h5><p>Students must possess the autonomy to retract pending applications if their academic schedule conflicts or if they accept alternative assistantships. We extended the application status enum to include <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>withdrawn</code>. When a student withdraws their application, all evaluation notes, interview schedules, and availability heatmaps are locked in archive mode rather than purged. Should the student wish to re-apply later, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>ApplicationService::create_application()</code> now leverages atomic <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE</code> to smoothly re-activate the application record without unique constraint collisions.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-shield-slash-fill text-accent me-2''></i>3. Account Suspension &amp; Administrative Restoration Authority</h5><p>To address non-compliant user accounts without corrupting student records or employer job listings, we implemented account deactivation via <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>suspend_user()</code> and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>reactivate_user()</code> in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>user-service.php</code>. Suspended users are immediately denied access across all login checkpoints with an informative institutional deactivation notice. Crucially, to prevent unauthorized data resurrection, restoration privileges (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>restore_job</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>restore_category</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>restore_career_update</code>) are restricted exclusively to institutional administrators.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-envelope-check-fill text-accent me-2''></i>4. Frictionless Defense Evaluation: In-Session OTP Passcode Fallback</h5><p>During the live capstone evaluation and local defense presentations, access to external internet SMTP relays (e.g. Gmail or SendGrid) may be restricted or firewalled on campus Wi-Fi. To guarantee zero presentation downtime, we enhanced <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>SessionGuard</code> and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>verify-email.php</code>: when outbound SMTP is unconfigured in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>.env</code>, the cryptographic 6-digit verification OTP is securely passed to <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>$_SESSION[''pending_verification''][''dev_code'']</code> and cleanly rendered within a testing mode banner on screen. This enables frictionless evaluation while strictly preserving the authentic multi-step verification quarantine state machine.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-shield-lock-fill text-accent me-2''></i>5. Defense-in-Depth Security Shielding &amp; Environment Standardization</h5><p>We completed three critical security shielding operations: First, we introduced <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>mask_ai_api_key()</code> in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>includes/ai/security.php</code>, preventing NVIDIA NIM API keys from being exposed in DOM text or browser inspector tools. Second, we deployed <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>database/.htaccess</code>, blocking all direct HTTP web access to SQL schemas, database dumps, logs, and seed files. Third, we standardized database environment loading in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>includes/db.php</code> via <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>.env</code>, ensuring clean separation between local development and production deployment parameters.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-journal-code text-accent me-2''></i>6. Complete Obsidian Defense Knowledge Vault (docs/codebase/)</h5><p>To prepare our six-member engineering team for the BSIS201 Midterm and Capstone Defense, we built an exhaustive, Obsidian-compatible documentation vault under <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>docs/codebase/</code>. Structured around a Master Map of Content (MOC), the vault provides architectural sequence diagrams, line-by-line function breakdowns, security audits, and high-yield defense Q&amp;A talking points for every single controller, service, and template across all five architectural layers. With 100% test coverage and full audit preservation, KLD Campus Hire stands fully prepared for panel defense.</p>","key_takeaways":["Replaced all destructive DELETE operations across categories, jobs, bulletins, and users with non-destructive soft-delete archival flags (is_archived, archived_at).","Empowered student applicants with audit-preserved application withdrawal (withdrawn) and frictionless re-submission via ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE.","Engineered administrative-only restoration privileges to prevent accidental data resurrection by unauthorized actors.","Integrated a testing-mode OTP verification fallback in SessionGuard and view templates, eliminating external SMTP dependencies during defense evaluation.","Hardened security posture via NVIDIA NIM API key masking (mask_ai_api_key), Apache .htaccess protection for database dumps, and .env configuration loading.","Delivered a complete Obsidian-compatible defense vault (docs/codebase/) containing architecture flows, security breakdowns, and panel Q&A talking points for 50+ files."],"tech_stack":["PHP 8.2 & MySQL Relational Schema","Non-Destructive Soft-Delete Pattern","MySQL ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE","Role-Based Restoration RBAC","Apache Directory Shielding (.htaccess)","API Key Cryptographic Masking","Obsidian Markdown Knowledge Vault"]}','2026-09-29 12:00:00'),('day-25','25','3D Mascot Architecture: Mesh Decimation, Geometry Pre-Cleaning & Unlocking Hardware-Accelerated WebGL for Hosted Production','October 1, 2026','Overcame our final production asset barrier by diagnosing and compressing the platform''s 54MB interactive 3D robot mascot down to a lean 7.45MB (an 86.2% size reduction). Stripped out 20 redundant secondary meshes that were previously rejected client-side via runtime JavaScript loops, decimated 1.43 million microscopic triangles down to 168k with 0.1% geometric error tolerance, eliminated unused UV texture coordinates, preserved mathematical coordinate invariants for procedural OLED eye and mouth gaze kinematics, and unlocked hardware-accelerated 3D WebGL across hosted production environments previously constrained by the 10MB upload threshold.','{"id":"day-25","sprint_number":"25","sprint_badge":"DAY 25 · 3D WEBGL ASSET COMPRESSION, GEOMETRIC DECIMATION & PRODUCTION DEPLOYMENT","title":"3D Mascot Architecture: Mesh Decimation, Geometry Pre-Cleaning & Unlocking Hardware-Accelerated WebGL for Hosted Production","date":"October 1, 2026","read_time":"10 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Overcame our final production asset barrier by diagnosing and compressing the platform''s 54MB interactive 3D robot mascot down to a lean 7.45MB (an 86.2% size reduction). Stripped out 20 redundant secondary meshes that were previously rejected client-side via runtime JavaScript loops, decimated 1.43 million microscopic triangles down to 168k with 0.1% geometric error tolerance, eliminated unused UV texture coordinates, preserved mathematical coordinate invariants for procedural OLED eye and mouth gaze kinematics, and unlocked hardware-accelerated 3D WebGL across hosted production environments previously constrained by the 10MB upload threshold.","tags":["3D WebGL Performance","GLTF/GLB Asset Decimation","Meshoptimizer & Vertex Welding","Three.js Kinematics Invariants","Client-Side CPU Optimization","Production Asset Deployment","InfinityFree Storage Compliance"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-25.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>As we enter final production staging for the KLD Campus Job Posting System, Day 25 resolves the single largest asset bottleneck in the repository: our 54.15MB interactive 3D hero mascot (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>cute_robot.glb</code>). Previously, the sheer weight of this asset prevented its deployment to our free hosted production cluster (InfinityFree), which strictly enforces a 10MB single-file upload threshold. Today, our engineering team engineered a lossless asset pipeline that compressed the 3D model by 86.2% down to 7.45MB, eliminated expensive client-side geometry rejection loops, verified mathematical coordinate invariants for procedural eye and mouth kinematics, and enabled hardware-accelerated Three.js 3D rendering for hosted users worldwide.</p><p>Interactive 3D web mascots provide unmatched engagement when greeting students and campus recruiters, but 3D assets on the web frequently suffer from unoptimized DCC (digital content creation) exports. A comprehensive binary audit of <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>cute_robot.glb</code> revealed three systemic inefficiencies that inflated the binary to over 54MB.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-search text-accent me-2''></i>1. The 54MB Asset Audit &amp; Ghost Geometry Discovery</h5><p>Using <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>@gltf-transform/cli</code> and custom binary buffer inspectors, we analyzed the internal chunk structure of the original 54.15MB GLB container. We uncovered that the file contained <strong>zero image textures</strong>—the entire 54MB consisted exclusively of raw floating-point vertex positions, normals, and index buffers across 42 distinct mesh nodes.</p><p>Crucially, we discovered that the source GLB actually bundled <em>two separate robots</em> (the primary mascot and a miniature companion) as well as an expansive front-stage floor tray. On every client visit, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>hero-robot.js</code> was downloading all 54MB across the network and then running heavy JavaScript loops (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>fullyRemovedMeshIndices</code> and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>partiallySharedMeshIndices</code>) to prune 20 full meshes and slice off triangles with coordinate predicates (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>x &gt;= 1.15</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>y &lt;= -1.65</code>). Over 28MB of transmitted data was discarded by client CPU immediately after download!</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-scissors text-accent me-2''></i>2. Headless Geometry Pre-Cleaning &amp; UV Stripping</h5><p>Rather than penalizing mobile clients and low-bandwidth connections with runtime mesh excision, we built a headless Node/Bun pipeline leveraging Three.js <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>GLTFLoader</code> and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>GLTFExporter</code>. The pipeline pre-evaluated the exact triangle rejection rules, extracted only the primary mascot (reducing 42 meshes to 22 clean nodes), and stripped unused <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>TEXCOORD_0</code> UV channels that were consuming 8 bytes per vertex without any backing textures. This single offline pass sliced the file size from <strong>54.15MB to 21.57MB</strong> before any geometry simplification was applied.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-cpu text-accent me-2''></i>3. Meshoptimizer Decimation &amp; Precision Preservation</h5><p>The remaining solo model contained 708,366 triangles with sub-millimeter vertex density far beyond standard screen resolution limits. We chained meshoptimizer vertex welding and quadric error decimation:</p><ul><li><strong>Vertex Welding:</strong> Merged coincident duplicate vertices, reducing un-indexed boundaries and lowering size to 17.98MB.</li><li><strong>Geometric Simplification:</strong> Decimated triangles from 708k down to 168k while locking boundary vertices and enforcing an ultra-tight error tolerance of 0.1% (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>--error 0.001</code>). This preserved the organic curvature of the head capsule, joint spheres, and polished breastplate with zero polygonal faceting.</li></ul><p>The resulting standard GLB registered at <strong>7.45MB</strong>—comfortably below the 10MB ceiling without requiring external WASM runtime decoders or non-standard GLTF extensions.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-eye-fill text-accent me-2''></i>4. Mathematical Verification of Kinematics Invariants</h5><p>The mascot''s interactive charm relies on 13 procedural kinematics in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>hero-robot.js</code>: real-time cursor gaze tracking, blinks, winks, wide excitement, and speaking mouth oscillations. These behaviors rely on dynamic pivot math pinned to specific geometry centroids: <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>Object_34</code> (right eye), <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>Object_41</code> (left eye), and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>Object_37</code> (digital mouth).</p><p>We executed automated simulation assertions comparing the centroid vectors between the uncompressed and compressed models:</p><ul><li><strong>Left Eye Centroid (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>Object_41</code>):</strong> Matched exactly at <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>[-0.134, -1.339, 1.488]</code>.</li><li><strong>Right Eye Centroid (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>Object_34</code>):</strong> Matched exactly at <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>[0.415, -1.243, 1.501]</code>.</li><li><strong>Mouth Centroid (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>Object_37</code>):</strong> Matched exactly at <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>[0.144, -1.253, 1.236]</code>.</li></ul><p>Furthermore, because the ghost secondary robot was removed offline, the geometric center of the mascot corrected from <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>x = 0.50</code> to <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>x = -0.01</code>, naturally centering the robot on the hero canvas without manual offset hacks.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-cloud-arrow-up-fill text-accent me-2''></i>5. Production Deployment Enablement &amp; CLI FTP Integration</h5><p>With the model reduced to 7.45MB, we updated the platform runtime architecture across three critical seams:</p><ul><li><strong><code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>includes/components.php</code>:</strong> Introduced <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>is_3d_robot_enabled()</code>, unlocking interactive 3D WebGL rendering across hosted production environments by default while preserving lightweight photo mode as an opt-in toggle (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>?mode_photo</code> or <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>ENABLE_3D_ROBOT=false</code>).</li><li><strong><code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>index.php</code> &amp; <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>faqs.php</code>:</strong> Updated script dependency loading to deliver Three.js and GLTFLoader on all 3D-enabled environments.</li><li><strong><code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>tools/deploy.py</code>:</strong> Removed <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>cute_robot.glb</code> from the exclusion blacklist, enabling frictionless one-command FTP synchronization to InfinityFree (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>ftpupload.net</code>).</li></ul><p>With an 86.2% smaller footprint, zero frame drops on client devices, and instant 3D interactivity across both local and hosted deployments, KLD Campus Hire delivers an enterprise-grade visual experience without compromising bandwidth or accessibility.</p>","key_takeaways":["Compressed interactive 3D mascot cute_robot.glb by 86.2% from 54.15MB down to 7.45MB, comfortably clearing the 10MB hosting threshold.","Eliminated client-side CPU overhead by pre-cleaning 20 redundant secondary meshes and stage trays offline instead of parsing and stripping them via runtime JavaScript.","Decimated 1.43M raw triangles to 168k with 0.1% geometric error tolerance, preserving pristine organic bevels and curved surfaces.","Stripped unreferenced TEXCOORD_0 UV coordinates across 22 meshes, saving 8 bytes per vertex on procedural PBR materials.","Mathematically validated coordinate invariants for eye (Object_34, Object_41) and mouth (Object_37) tracking pivots to 3 decimal places.","Updated includes/components.php, index.php, and faqs.php with is_3d_robot_enabled(), unlocking 3D WebGL on hosted servers while maintaining photo fallback.","Updated tools/deploy.py to sync the compressed 3D mascot directly to InfinityFree via automated CLI FTP."],"tech_stack":["Three.js r128 & WebGL Engine","GLTF 2.0 Binary Format (GLB)","Meshoptimizer Decimation & Vertex Welding","@gltf-transform/cli Pipeline","Procedural Kinematics & OLED Visor Shaders","PHP 8.2 Environment Configuration","Automated Python CLI FTP Deployment"]}','2026-09-30 12:00:00'),('day-26','26','Holistic Brand Harmony: Theme-Aware D4 Antenna Iconography, Universal Settings Gateway Routing & Admin Verification Triage with Actionable Feedback','October 3, 2026','Elevated the platform''s brand identity, settings ergonomics, and administrative verification governance: transitioned from generic SVG placeholders to the official dual-theme D4 Antenna Helper mascot identity and dynamic browser favicons; unified cross-role account configuration via centralized settings gateway routers; and re-engineered administrative credential review with contextual rejection accordions and actionable revision feedback.','{"id":"day-26","sprint_number":"26","sprint_badge":"DAY 26 · DUAL-THEME BRAND IDENTITY, SETTINGS UNIFICATION, ADMIN REJECTION REASONING & REVISION TRIAGE","title":"Holistic Brand Harmony: Theme-Aware D4 Antenna Iconography, Universal Settings Gateway Routing & Admin Verification Triage with Actionable Feedback","date":"October 3, 2026","read_time":"9 min read","author_name":"Alwinson Bustamante","author_role":"Lead Developer & System Architect","author_image":"assets/img/developers/BUSTAMANTE.jpg","summary_excerpt":"Elevated the platform''s brand identity, settings ergonomics, and administrative verification governance: transitioned from generic SVG placeholders to the official dual-theme D4 Antenna Helper mascot identity and dynamic browser favicons; unified cross-role account configuration via centralized settings gateway routers; and re-engineered administrative credential review with contextual rejection accordions and actionable revision feedback.","tags":["Brand Identity & Favicons","Dynamic Theme Pairing","Universal Settings Gateway","Admin Verification Triage","Contextual Rejection Notes","Document Path Resolution","Production Synchronization"],"cover_image":"assets/img/devblog/day-26.jpg","full_story":"<p class=''lead text-ink fw-semibold''>Day 26 brings a unified standard of design maturity, account governance, and administrative verification across the entire KLD Campus Job Posting System. We transitioned the portal from legacy geometric SVG placeholder icons to our authentic dual-theme D4 Antenna Helper mascot iconography, eliminated routing fragmentation by centralizing settings gateways across all user roles, and transformed administrative credential review from a blunt decline into an empathetic, actionable revision triage workflow.</p><p>As an institutional system preparing for full academic deployment, every touchpoint must convey institutional credibility, visual cohesion, and transparent user feedback. Today''s sprint systematically addresses the remaining user-experience friction points across branding, configuration navigation, and credential auditing.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-palette-fill text-accent me-2''></i>1. Dual-Theme D4 Antenna Brand Identity &amp; Dynamic Favicon Ecosystem</h5><p>Previously, the main navigation bar, login split shell, and shared footer displayed generic green geometric polyline SVGs. While functional, they failed to reinforce our university mascot identity established in the 3D hero stage. We replaced these with the high-resolution, pixel-crisp <strong>D4 Antenna Helper brand mark</strong> (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>logo-d4-light-64.png</code> and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>logo-d4-dark-64.png</code>).</p><p>To guarantee instantaneous, zero-flicker theme synchronization, we implemented an in-head theme sniffer and integrated <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>syncBrandLogo(theme)</code> directly into <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>assets/js/theme-toggle.js</code>. Whenever a user toggles between Paper Parchment (light) and Obsidian Cyberpunk (dark) modes—or when the browser evaluates OS-level <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>prefers-color-scheme</code>—the brand marks across the navbar, login panel, and footer swap synchronously. Concurrently, the engine dynamically repoints the browser tab favicon link tags (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>favicon-32.png</code>, <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>favicon-16.png</code>, and dark variants) and sets the mobile viewport <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>&lt;meta name=\\"theme-color\\"&gt;</code> to match the active background canvas.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-gear-wide-connected text-accent me-2''></i>2. Universal Settings Gateway Routing</h5><p>In our modular architecture, role-specific account management previously exhibited fragmented paths. While administrative and core profile settings resided in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>settings.php</code>, employer and student dashboard navigation buttons periodically targeted hypothetical child routes like <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>employer/settings.php</code> and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>student/settings.php</code>. Rather than duplicating dense configuration forms or risking HTTP 404 dead ends, we engineered dedicated routing gateways for both roles. These gateway controllers enforce strict authentication assertions via <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>require_auth()</code> and cleanly dispatch requests to the root settings center with persistent session preservation. We also registered these routes in our automated runtime page verification suite (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>tools/test-runtime-pages.php</code>), maintaining 100% test suite coverage.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-shield-check text-accent me-2''></i>3. Administrative Verification Triage &amp; Actionable Revision Feedback</h5><p>A crucial institutional requirement under campus employment policies is thorough credential verification for student assistants (via Certificates of Registration / COR) and campus employers (via department accreditations and business permits). Previously, administrative rejection in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>admin/users.php</code> was a binary, abrupt action with a generic static flash message. This left rejected students and employers confused as to why their registration was declined.</p><p>We completely overhauled this workflow in <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>includes/templates/admin-users-view.php</code> by introducing an interactive Bootstrap 5 collapse rejection drawer (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>#rejectPanelStudent</code> and <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>#rejectPanelEmp</code>). When an administrator clicks <em>Reject / Request Revision</em>, an inline contextual input panel smoothly expands, allowing the administrator to input explicit, tailored revision instructions (such as ''Illegible COR copy'', ''Student ID mismatch with registered degree program'', or ''Expired departmental accreditation permit''). The server controller captures and records these specific notes into the audit trail, dispatching real-time notifications so candidates can immediately correct and resubmit their credentials without administrative deadlock.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-folder-check text-accent me-2''></i>4. Robust Relative-Path Proof File Resolution</h5><p>During adversarial document verification audits, we identified that student verification modals occasionally failed to preview uploaded PDFs and image proof files due to fragile relative directory traversing in nested admin views. We modernized the document disk probe to use robust, root-anchored filesystem resolution (<code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>dirname(__DIR__, 2) . ''/'' . ltrim((string)$proof_doc, ''/'')</code>). Both multi-page PDF documents and graphic certificate scans now render reliably in administrative review modals regardless of calling depth.</p><h5 class=''fw-bold text-ink mt-4 mb-2''><i class=''bi bi-arrow-repeat text-accent me-2''></i>5. Automated Production Branch Synchronization</h5><p>To eliminate manual drift between development iterations and our live hosting mirror, we finalized <code class=''bg-cream text-ink px-1 rounded''>tools/deploy_main_sync.py</code>. This automated deployment orchestrator verifies clean working tree states, enforces strict file exclusion blacklists (protecting local environment credentials and scratch logs), and synchronizes validated production commits seamlessly to the remote repository.</p>","key_takeaways":["Replaced static SVG marks with theme-aware D4 Antenna Helper logos across navbar, login, and footer with zero visual flicker.","Integrated dynamic brand logo and favicon pairing into theme-toggle.js, adapting in real time to user preference and system dark mode.","Established seamless settings gateway routers (employer/settings.php, student/settings.php) routing to centralized account management.","Overhauled admin user verification with contextual collapse panels, enabling specific, actionable revision notes upon credential rejection.","Hardened disk path resolution for student COR and employer accreditation documents across nested templates.","Validated all 32 core runtime pages with 0 warnings or errors in tools/test-runtime-pages.php."],"tech_stack":["Vanilla JS Theme Engine","Dual-Theme Visual Branding","PHP Gateway Routing","Bootstrap 5 Collapse Drawers","Verification State Machine","Dynamic Favicon Swapping","Python Deployment Sync"]}','2026-10-02 12:00:00');
